WEBVTT

1
00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.611
Well, well, Boris the Animal has a visitor.

2
00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.068
I guess one every 40 years is okay.

3
00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:08.569
It's a cake.

4
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.829
I decide what it is.

5
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:15.956
Looks like some kind of cake.

6
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.836
She's clean.
Well, not clean, but you know...

7
00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.620
Oh, God.

8
00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:09.421
Boris the Animal...

9
00:02:10.047 --> 00:02:11.469
...you've got a visitor.

10
00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:15.018
It's just Boris.

11
00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.853
Your letters have been
a soul-nourishing...

12
00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:24.770
...tοnic.

13
00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:29.654
And you are much more...

14
00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:34.367
...unconventionally handsome
than your photos.

15
00:02:44.373 --> 00:02:46.125
This ain't a conjugal visit.

16
00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:47.668
So quit your conjugating.

17
00:02:48.919 --> 00:02:52.139
When's the last time
you conjugated anything?

18
00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:54.637
I see you've brought me a treat, darling.

19
00:02:55.258 --> 00:02:57.932
Would you mind cutting this up
for us? It's a special day.

20
00:02:58.428 --> 00:03:00.772
I'm a romantic like that.

21
00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:07.487
Oh, I wouldn't do that.

22
00:03:07.646 --> 00:03:08.317
Why's that?

23
00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.232
It'll ruin your figure.

24
00:03:55.193 --> 00:03:57.537
You complete me.

25
00:04:16.339 --> 00:04:17.431
The big one.

26
00:04:22.721 --> 00:04:24.723
Boris! You promised
to take me with you!

27
00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:25.982
We had a deal!

28
00:04:28.351 --> 00:04:30.353
Obadiah Price.

29
00:04:31.521 --> 00:04:35.151
Yes. I did make you a promise.

30
00:04:43.742 --> 00:04:46.461
Wait. I smell something.

31
00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:54.211
You can't win, Boris.

32
00:04:54.503 --> 00:04:56.176
Let's agree to disagree.

33
00:04:56.338 --> 00:04:57.260
There's too many of us.

34
00:04:57.422 --> 00:05:01.177
Rather hot in here.
Mind if I open a window?

35
00:05:19.778 --> 00:05:23.078
Sorry, darling.
We did love the cake.

36
00:05:45.679 --> 00:05:49.400
Let's rewrite history, shall we, K?

37
00:06:10.078 --> 00:06:11.045
Good afternoon.

38
00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.923
Please give your attention
to my associate, Agent J.

39
00:06:14.082 --> 00:06:16.710
He's going to demonstrate
an electro-biomechanical...

40
00:06:16.877 --> 00:06:19.505
...neural-transmitting,
zero-synapse repositioner.

41
00:06:19.671 --> 00:06:20.888
We call it the neuralyser.

42
00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:23.345
- Keep it simple, slick.
- Thanks a lot.

43
00:06:23.592 --> 00:06:24.639
Thank you, Agent K.

44
00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:27.099
Ladies and gentlemen,
if you will look right here.

45
00:06:30.098 --> 00:06:33.853
You know how you're on a plane and
you're asked to turn your phone off?

46
00:06:34.019 --> 00:06:37.239
You're like, "I ain't turning it off.
Has nothing to do with a plane."

47
00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:39.820
Well, this is what we get.
That's what happens.

48
00:06:39.983 --> 00:06:43.203
It gets up there, bounces around
on the satellites and:

49
00:06:43.361 --> 00:06:44.783
Just turn your damn phone off.

50
00:06:44.946 --> 00:06:48.246
Now you're gonna drive off a cliff
tonight because your GPS don't work.

51
00:06:49.618 --> 00:06:52.462
Check the composition
of the fuel units and surface deposits.

52
00:06:52.621 --> 00:06:53.998
I wanna know who was driving.

53
00:06:54.164 --> 00:06:55.586
Yes, sir.

54
00:06:55.749 --> 00:06:57.968
- What are you gonna say tonight?
- Don't worry.

55
00:06:58.126 --> 00:06:59.969
No, I'm very worried.
This is important.

56
00:07:00.128 --> 00:07:02.847
- I'm hungry. You hungry?
- K.

57
00:07:03.006 --> 00:07:05.680
Seriously, I'm not even sure that's meat.

58
00:07:05.842 --> 00:07:09.187
I think I just saw a tooth in that thing.
Or a claw. Or a hoof.

59
00:07:09.346 --> 00:07:10.848
Thanks, Manny.

60
00:07:11.014 --> 00:07:13.517
That does not belong in a pita,
it belongs in a casket.

61
00:07:13.683 --> 00:07:15.902
What would go good with this
would be silence.

62
00:07:16.061 --> 00:07:17.233
See, here's the problem.

63
00:07:17.395 --> 00:07:18.567
You can't smell it...

64
00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.825
...because your nose already
smells like that, but my nose doesn't.

65
00:07:21.983 --> 00:07:26.033
Silence goes good with a lot of things.
Ever try or is talking how you breathe?

66
00:07:26.196 --> 00:07:28.870
Just say you hate me.
Don't take it out on the car.

67
00:07:29.032 --> 00:07:30.409
Let me enjoy this.

68
00:07:30.575 --> 00:07:32.202
Whoa, enjoyment.

69
00:07:32.369 --> 00:07:35.748
So that's what enjoyment looks like
on that face. I like that emotion.

70
00:07:36.915 --> 00:07:38.132
I keep emotion out of it.

71
00:07:38.667 --> 00:07:40.795
Out of what, K? Life?

72
00:07:43.171 --> 00:07:44.593
You don't wanna run it by me?

73
00:07:44.756 --> 00:07:46.724
- Let me know what you'll say?
- Don't worry.

74
00:07:46.883 --> 00:07:49.306
Oh, no, I'm worried. Very worried.

75
00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:51.892
It's the man's eulogy.
You have to show some feeling.

76
00:07:52.764 --> 00:07:55.608
That thing people do when they
change their facial expression?

77
00:07:56.518 --> 00:07:58.862
I worked with Zed for 40 years.
A hell of an agent.

78
00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.944
And I have written
a hell of a speech for him.

79
00:08:02.107 --> 00:08:03.529
People will be moved.

80
00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.514
And now a few words from Agent K.

81
00:08:27.048 --> 00:08:29.927
I worked with Zed for over 40 years,
and in all that time...

82
00:08:30.093 --> 00:08:31.720
...he never invited me to dinner.

83
00:08:32.053 --> 00:08:35.648
He never asked me to his house
to watch a game.

84
00:08:36.474 --> 00:08:39.899
He never shared a single detail
of his personal life.

85
00:08:40.603 --> 00:08:42.321
Yeah, he was weird.

86
00:08:47.402 --> 00:08:48.745
Thank you.

87
00:08:50.697 --> 00:08:53.951
And now we will hear from
our new chief, Agent O.

88
00:08:54.117 --> 00:08:56.415
Thank you, Agent K.
That was very moving.

89
00:08:56.578 --> 00:08:59.707
- That was your eulogy?
- He was a good man.

90
00:08:59.873 --> 00:09:03.002
Ladies, gentlemen, other life forms.

91
00:09:03.418 --> 00:09:07.173
When I told the Finucian Zyglot
about Zed's passing...

92
00:09:07.338 --> 00:09:09.591
...she said something
that I'm going to repeat.

93
00:09:10.091 --> 00:09:11.809
And I'm paraphrasing.

94
00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:37.452
That's just so Zed.

95
00:09:38.119 --> 00:09:39.666
Thank you.

96
00:09:51.716 --> 00:09:53.343
You lose something over here, Hondo?

97
00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:57.105
Can you promise, if I go first, you'll
do better than that at my funeral?

98
00:09:57.263 --> 00:09:59.311
You know, something like:

99
00:09:59.474 --> 00:10:01.351
"J was a friend.

100
00:10:01.518 --> 00:10:04.522
Now there's a big part of me that's gone.

101
00:10:04.687 --> 00:10:08.032
Oh, J, all the things
that I should have said...

102
00:10:08.191 --> 00:10:10.444
...except I was too old...

103
00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.408
...and craggy and surly...

104
00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:14.868
...and just tight. I was too...

105
00:10:15.031 --> 00:10:16.578
...tight.

106
00:10:16.741 --> 00:10:20.666
I'm gonna just miss
your caramel-brown skin."

107
00:10:20.829 --> 00:10:22.547
I'll wing something.

108
00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:28.633
<i>K, it's O. We have reports
of several humans suffering from...</i>

109
00:10:28.795 --> 00:10:31.548
<i>...intestinal worms of alien origin.</i>

110
00:10:31.714 --> 00:10:32.761
Thank you, O.

111
00:10:34.342 --> 00:10:36.094
How did you get to be like you?

112
00:10:36.261 --> 00:10:38.059
Something happened, K.
What happened?

113
00:10:38.513 --> 00:10:40.311
You know how I live such a happy life?

114
00:10:40.849 --> 00:10:43.352
How you live such a happy life?

115
00:10:43.601 --> 00:10:46.445
I don't ask questions
I don't want to know the answer to.

116
00:10:47.772 --> 00:10:49.194
That's deep.

117
00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:01.753
Jeffrey.

118
00:11:04.455 --> 00:11:05.331
Do I know you?

119
00:11:05.623 --> 00:11:10.003
Your services are legendary.
So says your father, Obadiah.

120
00:11:10.545 --> 00:11:11.842
You were in Lunar-Max.

121
00:11:12.005 --> 00:11:15.600
There is no prison that can hold me.

122
00:11:16.718 --> 00:11:19.141
Cool for you.
What do you need from me, man?

123
00:11:19.304 --> 00:11:20.601
The device.

124
00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:25.356
I'm going back in time to kill a man
before he takes my arm.

125
00:11:41.826 --> 00:11:42.793
K, J!

126
00:11:42.994 --> 00:11:46.544
So happy to see you.
Mr. Wu get you your regular table?

127
00:11:54.088 --> 00:11:55.135
You no hungry?

128
00:11:55.298 --> 00:11:56.390
Show us the tanks, Wu.

129
00:11:56.758 --> 00:11:59.807
Oh, sure, sure. You look.
Very fresh.

130
00:11:59.969 --> 00:12:01.721
Show us the tanks in the back.

131
00:12:02.263 --> 00:12:05.187
So sorry. No speak English.
You come back later, okay?

132
00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.648
Save the chop-socky bullshit
for the tourists, Wu.

133
00:12:10.772 --> 00:12:13.400
Hey, what you guys
wanna bust my balls for, huh?

134
00:12:13.858 --> 00:12:15.110
You don't have no balls.

135
00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:21.328
Man, you look like
you come from the planet...

136
00:12:21.491 --> 00:12:22.583
...Damn.

137
00:12:22.951 --> 00:12:26.626
And Bob here is a clear violation
of Health Ordinance 32:

138
00:12:26.788 --> 00:12:30.167
Selling unlicenced extraterrestrial...

139
00:12:32.627 --> 00:12:33.753
...foodstuffs.

140
00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.342
That is an Earth fish.

141
00:12:35.713 --> 00:12:38.011
Very traditional in China.
You arrest me...

142
00:12:38.174 --> 00:12:39.221
...that's a hate crime!

143
00:12:39.384 --> 00:12:40.385
It would be...

144
00:12:40.551 --> 00:12:42.144
...if you were Chinese.

145
00:12:42.971 --> 00:12:44.723
K, come on. I got larvae to feed.

146
00:12:46.641 --> 00:12:48.063
Who is the Spiky Βulba for?

147
00:12:48.226 --> 00:12:49.148
Nobody.

148
00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:50.311
Who's it for?

149
00:12:50.478 --> 00:12:51.479
I keep them in case!

150
00:12:51.646 --> 00:12:53.023
- In case what?
- I don't know!

151
00:12:53.189 --> 00:12:54.111
Anybody!

152
00:12:54.274 --> 00:12:55.571
All right, you slug.

153
00:12:58.820 --> 00:12:59.662
Wu...

154
00:12:59.821 --> 00:13:03.416
...he and I are having issues right now,
but you shouldn't suffer for that.

155
00:13:03.574 --> 00:13:04.291
Thank you, J.

156
00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:07.579
So if you don't like getting
fish-slapped, keep to our agreement.

157
00:13:07.745 --> 00:13:10.373
Earth people get Earth fish.
Real Earth fish.

158
00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:13.965
On behalf of my pathetic self
and worthless children, you stay.

159
00:13:14.127 --> 00:13:17.677
Allow me most honourable benefit
of serving you favourite noodles, K?

160
00:13:17.839 --> 00:13:19.716
Don't nobody want your
nasty-ass noodles.

161
00:13:19.882 --> 00:13:21.600
You're a piece of shit, Wu.

162
00:13:21.968 --> 00:13:22.935
Shrimp and bok choy.

163
00:13:23.219 --> 00:13:25.642
We're gonna be here for a while.

164
00:13:40.611 --> 00:13:42.113
That was just mean.

165
00:13:42.613 --> 00:13:44.707
What you did to Wu back there.

166
00:13:45.533 --> 00:13:47.706
Snatched his skirt off.

167
00:13:47.869 --> 00:13:49.871
That's just disrespectful.

168
00:13:50.204 --> 00:13:51.877
I used to play a game with my dad:

169
00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.759
What'll You Have
For Your Last Meal.

170
00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:57.383
You could do worse than this.

171
00:13:59.714 --> 00:14:00.886
Okay.

172
00:14:02.425 --> 00:14:03.802
I played a game with my dad...

173
00:14:03.968 --> 00:14:05.015
...called catch.

174
00:14:05.178 --> 00:14:07.681
Except I'd throw the ball
and it'd just hit the wall...

175
00:14:07.847 --> 00:14:09.190
...because he wasn't there.

176
00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:11.233
Don't badmouth your old man.

177
00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:15.030
I'm not badmouthing him.
I just didn't really know him.

178
00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:16.731
It's not right.

179
00:14:16.898 --> 00:14:18.946
Damn right it's not.
A boy needs a father.

180
00:14:19.108 --> 00:14:21.327
Table one hasn't ordered a thing.
Table three...

181
00:14:21.486 --> 00:14:23.238
...just drank his fourth cup...

182
00:14:23.404 --> 00:14:25.702
...of duck sauce.

183
00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:30.127
<i>K, the crashed ship...</i>

184
00:14:30.286 --> 00:14:32.004
<i>...from this morning
was stolen from--</i>

185
00:14:32.163 --> 00:14:32.834
Lunar-Max.

186
00:14:32.997 --> 00:14:33.964
Boris the Animal.

187
00:14:34.123 --> 00:14:35.170
How did you know?

188
00:14:35.333 --> 00:14:36.801
He has a taste for Spiky Bulba.

189
00:14:37.293 --> 00:14:38.510
<i>Give us a minute, chief.</i>

190
00:14:40.838 --> 00:14:42.385
We're in a situation.

191
00:14:43.341 --> 00:14:44.308
Oh, yeah.

192
00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:46.511
I take the Chloropod.

193
00:14:46.677 --> 00:14:47.803
You take the Tarantabee.

194
00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:49.438
And the Hydronian over there.

195
00:14:49.639 --> 00:14:50.686
I'll take the kitchen.

196
00:14:50.848 --> 00:14:52.475
Meet you on the street.

197
00:14:52.934 --> 00:14:54.436
This is a very confusing time...

198
00:14:54.602 --> 00:14:55.899
...in my life.

199
00:15:15.998 --> 00:15:16.669
Hey.

200
00:15:31.848 --> 00:15:33.896
Keep your mouth closed,
keep your head down.

201
00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:02.567
Hello, K.

202
00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:06.822
Boris the Animal.

203
00:17:07.401 --> 00:17:09.574
It's just Boris.

204
00:17:09.737 --> 00:17:13.833
You haven't changed very much.
I see the arm I shot off is still shot off.

205
00:17:14.534 --> 00:17:16.411
Yes, my arm.

206
00:17:18.955 --> 00:17:21.003
We've thought about that moment...

207
00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:23.713
...every day for the last 40 years.

208
00:17:23.876 --> 00:17:25.924
Well, that's just not living a full life.

209
00:17:26.087 --> 00:17:28.806
I can promise you
it will be longer than yours.

210
00:17:28.965 --> 00:17:32.686
Lonelier too. Since you're
the last Boglodite standing.

211
00:17:32.969 --> 00:17:34.687
We'll see about that.

212
00:17:34.845 --> 00:17:38.600
But first,
I want the pleasure of killing you.

213
00:17:38.766 --> 00:17:39.892
Yo, K.

214
00:17:41.727 --> 00:17:43.729
- Where the hell have you been?
- Fishing.

215
00:18:01.747 --> 00:18:05.001
You don't know it, K,
but you're already dead.

216
00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.092
You all right?

217
00:18:23.603 --> 00:18:25.526
May I have everyone's attention, please?

218
00:18:29.942 --> 00:18:30.738
Thank you.

219
00:18:30.901 --> 00:18:33.996
You know how your kid won
the goldfish in that little baggie...

220
00:18:34.155 --> 00:18:36.749
...from the fair and you didn't
want it in your house...

221
00:18:36.907 --> 00:18:40.377
...so you told your kid it ran away
when you flushed it down the toilet?

222
00:18:40.536 --> 00:18:42.038
Well, this is what happens.

223
00:18:42.204 --> 00:18:45.424
Okay? See what I'm talking about?
Don't lie to your kids.

224
00:18:51.213 --> 00:18:54.308
Man, I am getting too old for this.

225
00:18:54.467 --> 00:18:56.811
I can only imagine how you feel.

226
00:18:56.969 --> 00:18:59.063
Boris the Animal.

227
00:18:59.221 --> 00:19:02.600
I put him away a long time ago.
It's the worst mistake I ever made.

228
00:19:02.892 --> 00:19:04.860
Why? Was he innocent?

229
00:19:05.144 --> 00:19:06.942
Should have killed him.

230
00:19:08.898 --> 00:19:11.117
- Well, shit, let's go get him.
- No.

231
00:19:11.567 --> 00:19:13.069
- No.
- Leave it alone.

232
00:19:13.235 --> 00:19:14.452
It's above your pay grade.

233
00:19:14.654 --> 00:19:16.372
We have the same pay grade.

234
00:19:16.739 --> 00:19:19.458
It has nothing to do with you.
Mind your own business.

235
00:19:20.159 --> 00:19:23.584
Okay, first of all, let's get a little bit
of that bass out your voice.

236
00:19:23.746 --> 00:19:27.296
Secondly, as long as Spikey Boy is
running around, this is my business.

237
00:19:27.458 --> 00:19:29.836
You forget about Boris
or my report will reflect...

238
00:19:30.002 --> 00:19:32.004
...that your conduct
has been unbecoming.

239
00:19:32.505 --> 00:19:35.509
Well, maybe my report
is gonna reflect some shit too, K.

240
00:19:35.675 --> 00:19:38.178
- You are suspended for two weeks.
- Bullshit.

241
00:19:38.344 --> 00:19:40.312
Four weeks.

242
00:19:41.097 --> 00:19:42.565
How about I quit?

243
00:19:42.723 --> 00:19:44.976
There are things out there
you don't need to know.

244
00:19:45.142 --> 00:19:48.191
That's not the lie you told me
when you recruited me.

245
00:19:58.447 --> 00:19:59.164
What up, pops?

246
00:19:59.323 --> 00:20:01.997
- Lose your partner?
- Yeah.

247
00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.834
<i>Next shuttle to Afazumba...</i>

248
00:20:05.996 --> 00:20:08.875
<i>...leaving in 22 minutes.</i>

249
00:20:21.262 --> 00:20:21.979
<i>Search...</i>

250
00:20:22.138 --> 00:20:23.139
...Boris the Animal.

251
00:20:23.305 --> 00:20:25.558
<i>Boris the Animal,
Boglodite assassin.</i>

252
00:20:25.725 --> 00:20:27.523
<i>Boglodites were a rogue alien race...</i>

253
00:20:27.685 --> 00:20:29.687
<i>...that consumed all planets
in their path.</i>

254
00:20:29.854 --> 00:20:31.731
<i>Boris the Animal was the only suspect...</i>

255
00:20:31.897 --> 00:20:34.070
<i>...in a series of alien murders
on Earth.</i>

256
00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.196
Incident report.

257
00:20:35.359 --> 00:20:36.906
<i>Boris the Animal was convicted...</i>

258
00:20:37.069 --> 00:20:40.915
<i>...for the following murders
that occurred on July 15,1969.</i>

259
00:20:41.115 --> 00:20:45.666
<i>Murder number one: Coney Island,
10:37 a.m. Roman the Fabulist.</i>

260
00:20:45.828 --> 00:20:47.956
<i>Murder number two: The Factory.</i>

261
00:20:48.122 --> 00:20:48.793
Refine search.

262
00:20:48.956 --> 00:20:49.832
Agent K.

263
00:20:49.999 --> 00:20:52.468
<i>Junior Agent K apprehended and arrested...</i>

264
00:20:52.626 --> 00:20:57.177
<i>...Boris the Animal on July 16,1969,
at Cape Canaveral, Florida.</i>

265
00:20:57.339 --> 00:20:58.761
- Cape Canaveral...
- <i>Agent K...</i>

266
00:20:58.924 --> 00:21:01.393
<i>...received highest commendation
for heroic action...</i>

267
00:21:01.552 --> 00:21:02.895
<i>...including implementation...</i>

268
00:21:03.053 --> 00:21:04.726
<i>...of the Arc Net Defence System...</i>

269
00:21:04.889 --> 00:21:07.392
<i>...which protected the Earth
from Boglodite invasion...</i>

270
00:21:07.558 --> 00:21:09.276
<i>...and led to the race's extinction.</i>

271
00:21:09.435 --> 00:21:10.436
Details.

272
00:21:10.686 --> 00:21:12.029
<i>Access restricted.</i>

273
00:21:13.189 --> 00:21:18.491
Excuse me? Clearance level
senior agent, class one. J.

274
00:21:18.652 --> 00:21:19.869
<i>Access denied.</i>

275
00:21:20.237 --> 00:21:21.534
What?

276
00:21:36.212 --> 00:21:40.262
So why this sudden interest
in your partner's old exploits?

277
00:21:40.674 --> 00:21:42.347
What happened between Boris and Κ?

278
00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:43.432
That's easy.

279
00:21:43.594 --> 00:21:45.642
K imprisoned Boris.
He put up the Arc Net.

280
00:21:45.805 --> 00:21:48.354
He protected the Earth from the Boglodites.

281
00:21:48.516 --> 00:21:50.109
He did his job.

282
00:21:51.519 --> 00:21:52.941
That's not what I'm asking.

283
00:21:53.103 --> 00:21:54.776
Cape Canaveral, what happened?

284
00:21:55.481 --> 00:21:57.734
Something that changed him.

285
00:21:58.234 --> 00:22:00.032
Leave it at that.

286
00:22:01.904 --> 00:22:04.327
So you two go way back, huh?

287
00:22:09.578 --> 00:22:11.580
That's classified.

288
00:22:12.081 --> 00:22:14.334
A word of advice, Agent J.

289
00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:18.130
Don't ask questions
you don't want to know the answer to.

290
00:22:20.089 --> 00:22:23.639
That's funny.
That is exactly what K said.

291
00:22:27.429 --> 00:22:29.557
He's a very wise man.

292
00:22:29.932 --> 00:22:32.060
Take the rest of the night off.

293
00:22:48.826 --> 00:22:49.497
What?

294
00:22:49.952 --> 00:22:52.250
Guess I owe you some answers, hoss.

295
00:22:52.413 --> 00:22:54.415
<i>What, you're feeling chatty
all of a sudden?</i>

296
00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:58.385
I can't talk right now. I've got secret
cases of my own I'm working on.

297
00:22:58.544 --> 00:23:00.797
I hate to tear you away
from your video game.

298
00:23:01.547 --> 00:23:02.890
All right, I'm hanging up.

299
00:23:03.132 --> 00:23:06.511
<i>You know the most destructive force
in the universe?</i>

300
00:23:07.803 --> 00:23:09.146
Sugar?

301
00:23:09.638 --> 00:23:11.140
<i>Regret.</i>

302
00:23:13.475 --> 00:23:15.398
You don't have to wait. Just talk.

303
00:23:15.561 --> 00:23:18.189
I promised you the secrets
of the universe. Nothing more.

304
00:23:18.439 --> 00:23:21.363
So there's secrets out there
the universe don't know about?

305
00:24:40.020 --> 00:24:41.146
Mommy.

306
00:24:58.414 --> 00:24:59.961
Can I help you?

307
00:25:03.419 --> 00:25:04.671
K?

308
00:25:05.254 --> 00:25:06.847
5K.

309
00:25:11.093 --> 00:25:12.845
I'm sorry, is that chocolate milk?

310
00:25:13.012 --> 00:25:15.891
Can I--? I'm so sorry.
I don't know what...

311
00:25:17.766 --> 00:25:19.894
Mommy, the president is drinking...

312
00:25:20.060 --> 00:25:22.313
...my milk.

313
00:25:23.772 --> 00:25:24.443
I'm sorry.

314
00:25:27.776 --> 00:25:29.995
He didn't say please.

315
00:25:43.959 --> 00:25:46.462
- K get in yet?
- Who?

316
00:25:46.628 --> 00:25:47.504
You new?

317
00:25:47.671 --> 00:25:50.345
Very funny, Agent J.

318
00:25:58.474 --> 00:26:01.273
J, everything you told me yesterday,
you were right as rain.

319
00:26:01.435 --> 00:26:04.029
- Thank God for that 10-hour stakeout.
- Whο are you?

320
00:26:04.188 --> 00:26:06.907
Exactly.
I feel like a whole new man today.

321
00:26:07.066 --> 00:26:10.866
Like this great weight has been lifted.
I've had anger issues my entire life...

322
00:26:11.028 --> 00:26:13.622
...but now I see I was mad at myself.
And my stepmom.

323
00:26:13.781 --> 00:26:15.783
Sir, I'm gonna need you to stop talking.

324
00:26:15.949 --> 00:26:18.247
It's like I closed this emotional window.

325
00:26:18.410 --> 00:26:20.458
But I threw a brick through that window.

326
00:26:20.621 --> 00:26:22.498
Thank you for handing me that brick, J.

327
00:26:22.664 --> 00:26:26.339
Whoever you are, give me five feet
or I'll pluck you in your throat.

328
00:26:28.087 --> 00:26:30.465
I'm gonna go
to the little Men's-in-Black room...

329
00:26:30.631 --> 00:26:34.181
...then we'll go find those morons
from Pox Ethera. Lunch is on me.

330
00:26:35.928 --> 00:26:37.054
Whο was that?

331
00:26:37.221 --> 00:26:40.145
Double A? Your partner.

332
00:26:42.684 --> 00:26:45.233
I need you to go get me some
chocolate milk, all right?

333
00:26:45.395 --> 00:26:48.069
Just a really big glass.
Have you seen K?

334
00:26:48.232 --> 00:26:49.779
Did he call in sick or anything?

335
00:26:49.942 --> 00:26:51.410
Who's K?

336
00:26:52.361 --> 00:26:54.830
All right, all right, go ahead, go ahead.

337
00:26:54.988 --> 00:26:55.739
K!

338
00:26:57.032 --> 00:26:58.158
All right.

339
00:26:58.450 --> 00:26:59.827
You got me.

340
00:26:59.993 --> 00:27:02.246
I'll give it to you.
It's funny, very elaborate.

341
00:27:02.412 --> 00:27:05.586
Oh, and all of you, fantastic performances.

342
00:27:05.749 --> 00:27:08.468
You waited 14 years
to develop a sense of humour...

343
00:27:08.627 --> 00:27:10.345
...but this is a good one.

344
00:27:10.504 --> 00:27:12.347
But I need you to come out here now...

345
00:27:12.506 --> 00:27:14.929
...because I'm starting
to get a little pissed off.

346
00:27:15.092 --> 00:27:17.390
Agent J, would you mind
keeping your voice down...

347
00:27:17.553 --> 00:27:19.430
...and telling me
who you're looking for?

348
00:27:19.596 --> 00:27:20.722
I'm looking for K.

349
00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:22.562
Who is K?

350
00:27:24.643 --> 00:27:26.020
You too? You too.

351
00:27:26.186 --> 00:27:28.154
I mean, who is he to you?

352
00:27:28.313 --> 00:27:29.439
My partner.

353
00:27:29.898 --> 00:27:32.117
Older gentleman, 110...

354
00:27:32.276 --> 00:27:33.323
...maybe 111 years old.

355
00:27:33.485 --> 00:27:38.457
Sort of a surly, Elvis thing happening
with him. He smiles like this.

356
00:27:39.408 --> 00:27:40.751
Seen him around?

357
00:27:43.245 --> 00:27:44.747
I'll take you to K.

358
00:27:44.913 --> 00:27:46.756
Thank you.

359
00:27:53.088 --> 00:27:55.557
- What is that supposed to be?
- That's K.

360
00:27:55.716 --> 00:27:57.810
He's been dead for over 40 years.

361
00:27:58.677 --> 00:28:02.398
Okay, see, the prerequisite for a joke
is that it be funny.

362
00:28:02.931 --> 00:28:04.308
It's never been funny.

363
00:28:09.897 --> 00:28:12.992
Computer, Agent K and Boris the Animal.

364
00:28:13.150 --> 00:28:15.869
<i>Men in Black incident report,
July, 1969.</i>

365
00:28:16.028 --> 00:28:17.200
<i>Location, Cape Canaveral.</i>

366
00:28:17.362 --> 00:28:19.740
<i>Perpetrator Boris the Animal
escaped and fled Εarth.</i>

367
00:28:19.907 --> 00:28:23.161
<i>Assumed to have returned to planet
Boglodotia 20 light-years away.</i>

368
00:28:23.327 --> 00:28:26.672
<i>Agent K pronounced dead at scene.
Awarded posthumous commendation...</i>

369
00:28:26.830 --> 00:28:29.754
<i>...for action which prevented
greater loss of human life.</i>

370
00:28:29.917 --> 00:28:31.419
That's not what happened.

371
00:28:31.585 --> 00:28:33.553
I looked at this report.
K put Boris away--

372
00:28:33.712 --> 00:28:36.682
- Agent Κ is dead.
- Well, I just talked to him last night.

373
00:28:36.840 --> 00:28:38.262
- You are imagining.
- I'm not.

374
00:28:38.425 --> 00:28:40.393
- I need a psych team up here.
- Yes, ma'am.

375
00:28:40.552 --> 00:28:44.398
Aqua Velva aftershave.
I didn't imagine that.

376
00:28:44.556 --> 00:28:49.107
Every stakeout,
endless hours of cowboy music.

377
00:28:49.269 --> 00:28:51.317
Every morning with his coffee...

378
00:28:51.480 --> 00:28:55.110
...he'd say, "I tell you something, slick.
This coffee tastes like dirt."

379
00:28:55.275 --> 00:28:57.494
And I was supposed to say,
"What do you expect?

380
00:28:57.653 --> 00:28:59.451
- It was ground this morning."
- "This morning."

381
00:28:59.821 --> 00:29:01.323
How do you know that?

382
00:29:01.573 --> 00:29:02.870
Chocolate milk, sir?

383
00:29:03.033 --> 00:29:06.537
Where you been, man?
It was like an hour ago.

384
00:29:08.121 --> 00:29:08.872
Wait.

385
00:29:09.039 --> 00:29:11.918
How long have you been craving
chocolatised dairy products?

386
00:29:12.084 --> 00:29:13.461
Just today.

387
00:29:14.211 --> 00:29:16.259
Are you experiencing headaches?
Dizziness?

388
00:29:16.421 --> 00:29:17.923
Loss of balance?

389
00:29:18.090 --> 00:29:19.592
Agitation? Depression?

390
00:29:19.841 --> 00:29:20.933
Hell, yeah.

391
00:29:22.427 --> 00:29:24.680
Two possibilities.
One is you've been bitten...

392
00:29:24.846 --> 00:29:26.348
...by a Hovartian brain tick...

393
00:29:26.515 --> 00:29:28.984
...and could die in horrible agony
at any moment.

394
00:29:30.602 --> 00:29:33.401
Damn it. It's not the tick.

395
00:29:33.563 --> 00:29:35.531
"Damn it, it's not the tick"?

396
00:29:35.691 --> 00:29:37.364
It's something worse than the tick?

397
00:29:39.861 --> 00:29:42.034
Your obsession
with chocolate milk indicates...

398
00:29:42.197 --> 00:29:44.791
...that you might be involved
in a temporal fracture.

399
00:29:44.992 --> 00:29:46.790
I don't know what you're talking about.

400
00:29:46.952 --> 00:29:49.375
Chocolate milk relieves
temporal-fracture headaches.

401
00:29:49.871 --> 00:29:51.214
What's a temporal fracture?

402
00:29:51.373 --> 00:29:52.374
A break in the timeline.

403
00:29:52.541 --> 00:29:53.508
Don't know what you mean.

404
00:29:53.667 --> 00:29:55.510
Time travel! Time travel.

405
00:29:55.961 --> 00:29:57.884
There's no such thing as time travel.

406
00:29:58.255 --> 00:29:59.723
- Well, there is.
- No.

407
00:29:59.881 --> 00:30:00.973
There's not.

408
00:30:01.133 --> 00:30:02.555
Because if there were...

409
00:30:02.843 --> 00:30:05.722
...a class-one senior agent
such as myself...

410
00:30:05.887 --> 00:30:08.436
...would have been aware of it,
wouldn't he have?

411
00:30:08.598 --> 00:30:11.147
Were it not classified
and way above his pay grade.

412
00:30:12.352 --> 00:30:13.524
You know, I need a raise.

413
00:30:13.979 --> 00:30:16.277
There was one man, scumbag, Obadiah Price.

414
00:30:16.440 --> 00:30:19.489
He figured it out, we busted him,
we made time travel illegal...

415
00:30:19.943 --> 00:30:23.197
...throughout the universe
and he is serving life on Lunar-Max.

416
00:30:23.488 --> 00:30:26.116
No-- That's where Boris
was locked up.

417
00:30:28.577 --> 00:30:30.375
If Boris worked out how to time jump...

418
00:30:30.537 --> 00:30:33.256
...he could seriously change
the course of history.

419
00:30:34.166 --> 00:30:36.635
<i>Attention.
Εarly warning system engaged.</i>

420
00:30:37.044 --> 00:30:39.763
<i>Inbound hostile warships
entering solar system.</i>

421
00:30:39.921 --> 00:30:41.969
<i>Boglodite markings and language detected.</i>

422
00:30:42.132 --> 00:30:45.602
Boglodite. Boris is a Boglodite,
but they're extinct.

423
00:30:45.761 --> 00:30:47.058
Apparently not.

424
00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:50.190
<i>Catastrophic Earth attack imminent.</i>

425
00:30:50.766 --> 00:30:52.063
Put up the Arc Net.

426
00:30:52.351 --> 00:30:54.945
- The what?
- The Arc Net. The defence system.

427
00:30:55.103 --> 00:30:56.776
K got it for the Boglodites.

428
00:30:58.023 --> 00:30:59.525
There is no K.

429
00:30:59.691 --> 00:31:01.989
He's been dead for over 40 years.

430
00:31:02.152 --> 00:31:05.782
No K. No defence system.

431
00:31:06.156 --> 00:31:07.703
Boris jumped back and killed him.

432
00:31:07.866 --> 00:31:10.790
If you wanna save the world,
stop that from happening.

433
00:31:11.203 --> 00:31:13.626
You have to find Jeffrey Price.
He's Obadiah's son.

434
00:31:13.914 --> 00:31:16.292
Let's hope the little squirt
hasn't skipped town.

435
00:31:18.794 --> 00:31:22.424
- Good luck, J!
- This planet's toast.

436
00:31:39.272 --> 00:31:41.650
How can I help you?
We're having an amazing sale...

437
00:31:41.817 --> 00:31:42.488
...on batteries.

438
00:31:42.651 --> 00:31:45.279
Okay, we got other stuff,
like headphones, adapters or--

439
00:31:45.654 --> 00:31:47.406
You helped Boris the Animal time jump.

440
00:31:47.656 --> 00:31:49.658
Okay, I had to. That dude's a freak.

441
00:31:49.825 --> 00:31:50.826
He killed my partner.

442
00:31:50.992 --> 00:31:53.370
I want to know when and where you sent him.

443
00:31:53.537 --> 00:31:55.881
What, you think I keep, like, a logbook?

444
00:32:02.045 --> 00:32:03.467
Target vector, July 16...

445
00:32:03.630 --> 00:32:05.553
- ...1969.
- All right.

446
00:32:05.715 --> 00:32:07.467
That's a real bummer about your buddy.

447
00:32:07.634 --> 00:32:09.102
I'm sure he was a great guy.

448
00:32:09.261 --> 00:32:11.309
But in terms of
the space-time continuum...

449
00:32:11.471 --> 00:32:14.099
...your friend was a little blip
on the historical radar!

450
00:32:18.979 --> 00:32:20.947
That's a big blip.

451
00:32:21.857 --> 00:32:24.155
- Okay. What's the plan?
- Yοu're gonna send me...

452
00:32:24.317 --> 00:32:26.240
...back to July 15th, 1969.

453
00:32:26.403 --> 00:32:29.202
No, that's a stupid plan,
because I sent Boris to July 16th.

454
00:32:29.364 --> 00:32:32.243
I'm not worried about that one.
I'll kill the younger Boris...

455
00:32:32.409 --> 00:32:33.877
...before the older one shows.

456
00:32:34.035 --> 00:32:36.504
That way, neither of them will even exist.

457
00:32:36.663 --> 00:32:39.507
That's why you get to wear the black suit.

458
00:32:40.208 --> 00:32:40.925
No?

459
00:32:41.084 --> 00:32:43.212
You're gonna leave me hanging?
Okay.

460
00:32:43.378 --> 00:32:45.881
Oh, I just thought of something.
Even back then...

461
00:32:46.047 --> 00:32:48.141
...New York was like a big-ish city.

462
00:32:48.300 --> 00:32:50.223
So how are you gonna really find him?

463
00:32:50.385 --> 00:32:54.856
On July 15th, Boris killed an alien,
Roman the Fabulist, at Coney Island.

464
00:32:55.015 --> 00:32:57.188
You're gonna get there first
and be waiting?

465
00:32:57.350 --> 00:32:59.478
Dude, they should give you two black suits.

466
00:32:59.644 --> 00:33:00.896
My man, for real?

467
00:33:01.229 --> 00:33:01.946
Oh, right.

468
00:33:02.105 --> 00:33:03.357
Sorry.

469
00:33:04.232 --> 00:33:05.529
This...

470
00:33:05.734 --> 00:33:08.112
...is the real deal. Time-jump gear.

471
00:33:08.320 --> 00:33:09.993
Very rare, very old.

472
00:33:10.155 --> 00:33:12.328
But first, we gotta get high.

473
00:33:12.574 --> 00:33:13.871
Hey. No.

474
00:33:14.242 --> 00:33:16.711
No. No, I mean, really high.

475
00:33:38.517 --> 00:33:41.612
Hey, man? A little help here?

476
00:33:44.523 --> 00:33:45.649
Thank you.

477
00:33:45.815 --> 00:33:46.691
Okay.

478
00:33:47.859 --> 00:33:50.863
- You know the rules of time jumps?
- Give me the short version.

479
00:33:51.029 --> 00:33:53.828
Okay. You wanna save your partner,
word of advice:

480
00:33:53.990 --> 00:33:55.537
Stay away from him.

481
00:33:55.700 --> 00:33:58.203
Yeah, got it. Stay away from K.
Just kill Boris.

482
00:33:58.370 --> 00:34:00.213
Now, take these.

483
00:34:00.372 --> 00:34:02.124
It gets pretty windy on the way down.

484
00:34:03.375 --> 00:34:04.501
The way down?

485
00:34:04.668 --> 00:34:07.012
With eyes tearing up,
it's hard to read the dial.

486
00:34:07.170 --> 00:34:10.595
Plus, it helps you look like a real
time traveller, which is cool.

487
00:34:10.757 --> 00:34:12.851
I am not jumping off of this building!

488
00:34:13.009 --> 00:34:14.886
Time jump.

489
00:34:16.137 --> 00:34:16.933
Okay, now...

490
00:34:17.097 --> 00:34:18.895
...I gotta set this thing...

491
00:34:19.057 --> 00:34:20.650
...to the 15th.

492
00:34:22.185 --> 00:34:22.856
That seems...

493
00:34:23.019 --> 00:34:25.021
...right-ish.

494
00:34:26.398 --> 00:34:27.069
Now...

495
00:34:27.232 --> 00:34:29.701
...all you gotta do is jump.

496
00:34:29.859 --> 00:34:32.282
Hey, hey, stop. Stop it.

497
00:34:32.445 --> 00:34:34.163
When you're moving fast enough...

498
00:34:34.322 --> 00:34:37.872
...that circle is gonna fill up with
some sort of green time-travel liquid...

499
00:34:38.034 --> 00:34:39.786
...and it's gonna glow really bright.

500
00:34:39.953 --> 00:34:42.581
As soon as that happens,
break that blue laser line...

501
00:34:42.747 --> 00:34:44.715
...with your thumb
to complete the circuit.

502
00:34:44.874 --> 00:34:46.922
At this height, that should be...

503
00:34:47.085 --> 00:34:50.009
Let's see, mass of Earth
and 30-something feet per minute...

504
00:34:50.171 --> 00:34:52.640
It's 32 feet per second. Per second.

505
00:34:52.799 --> 00:34:54.767
That sounds right-ish.

506
00:34:54.926 --> 00:34:59.272
So that would be, I guess,
about two feet off the ground.

507
00:34:59.431 --> 00:35:00.728
I break the laser line?

508
00:35:00.890 --> 00:35:01.891
No, don't break it!

509
00:35:02.058 --> 00:35:04.026
- No, when I'm fast enough!
- Sounds good!

510
00:35:04.185 --> 00:35:07.109
Do I break the laser line
or do I not break the laser line?

511
00:35:07.272 --> 00:35:09.274
Do not lose that time device...

512
00:35:09.441 --> 00:35:13.412
...or you will be stuck in 1969!

513
00:35:13.570 --> 00:35:16.414
It wasn't the best time for your people.

514
00:35:17.616 --> 00:35:20.620
I'm just saying.
It's, like, a lot cooler now.

515
00:35:20.785 --> 00:35:22.332
How will I know if it works?

516
00:35:22.495 --> 00:35:24.338
You'll either know...

517
00:35:25.290 --> 00:35:26.837
...or you won't.

518
00:35:32.964 --> 00:35:35.217
You must really love this guy to do this.

519
00:35:35.383 --> 00:35:38.432
Oh, wait. How come I remember K,
but nobody else does?

520
00:35:41.598 --> 00:35:44.192
- That means you were there!
- I was where?

521
00:35:44.392 --> 00:35:47.316
If you survive, you gotta come back
and tell me everything.

522
00:35:47.479 --> 00:35:48.150
Where was I?

523
00:35:49.814 --> 00:35:50.815
You gotta go!

524
00:35:51.024 --> 00:35:51.775
Just go, go, go!

525
00:36:16.966 --> 00:36:18.092
Oh, no!

526
00:36:34.984 --> 00:36:35.826
Come on!

527
00:38:10.789 --> 00:38:13.759
- My man, what's today?
- Tuesday.

528
00:38:13.917 --> 00:38:15.419
- The date?
- The 15th.

529
00:38:15.585 --> 00:38:17.178
- Of?
- July.

530
00:38:17.337 --> 00:38:19.465
- Dog, the year.
- 1969.

531
00:38:19.631 --> 00:38:21.258
Thank you.

532
00:38:21.633 --> 00:38:23.886
Look at me like I'm crazy.

533
00:38:34.395 --> 00:38:35.362
Far out.

534
00:38:35.522 --> 00:38:37.991
Jerry rocked Haight-Ashbury
like you wouldn't believe.

535
00:38:46.825 --> 00:38:48.293
Okay, we're here.

536
00:38:48.451 --> 00:38:49.998
- Happy?
- Yοu're such a pill, Fred.

537
00:38:53.248 --> 00:38:55.671
- Get us checked in.
- Yeah, yeah.

538
00:38:56.918 --> 00:38:58.545
Hey. Hey, do me a favour, all right?

539
00:38:58.711 --> 00:39:00.930
- Be careful with the luggage.
- Absolutely, sir.

540
00:39:01.923 --> 00:39:04.267
I paid a lot of money for that luggage.

541
00:39:04.425 --> 00:39:06.974
- We'll take good care--
- Last time, it got scuffed up.

542
00:39:07.345 --> 00:39:10.599
Here you go, sir.
Just call down when you need it.

543
00:39:11.933 --> 00:39:13.230
There's more in the trunk.

544
00:39:13.393 --> 00:39:16.522
Yeah, it'll be in your room, sir.
Just go in.

545
00:39:16.688 --> 00:39:19.612
Excuse me. Excuse me, who is that?
Who are you?

546
00:39:26.781 --> 00:39:27.907
Let's go!

547
00:39:45.550 --> 00:39:46.972
Far out, man!

548
00:39:47.135 --> 00:39:49.888
If you want to keep that, I wouldn't.

549
00:39:50.054 --> 00:39:51.647
Make love, not war.

550
00:39:53.141 --> 00:39:55.189
I prefer to do both.

551
00:40:30.887 --> 00:40:32.935
How are you, officers?
What can I do you for?

552
00:40:33.097 --> 00:40:36.192
Well, look at this.
Power windows, power seats.

553
00:40:36.684 --> 00:40:38.482
- I'll bet you it cost 6 grand.
- Yeah.

554
00:40:38.645 --> 00:40:41.990
Yes, and it has a roof, but it's hidden.

555
00:40:42.357 --> 00:40:44.030
Hey, what kind of work do you do?

556
00:40:44.275 --> 00:40:45.492
An individual of your...

557
00:40:45.652 --> 00:40:48.576
...particular ethnic persuasion?

558
00:40:50.114 --> 00:40:52.492
Maybe he's a noted athlete.

559
00:40:53.284 --> 00:40:58.085
Yes. Starting forward
for the Detroit Darkies.

560
00:40:58.456 --> 00:41:00.504
- Where'd you get the car?
- And the suit?

561
00:41:00.708 --> 00:41:03.382
I stole them both.
Car from your wife...

562
00:41:03.544 --> 00:41:05.387
...suit from your grandmother.

563
00:41:07.215 --> 00:41:07.886
Hey.

564
00:41:08.049 --> 00:41:09.892
What do we have here?
Concealed weapon?

565
00:41:10.051 --> 00:41:11.769
Hey, it's his grandmother's suit.

566
00:41:12.136 --> 00:41:13.934
- Hey, what's this?
- Probably drugs.

567
00:41:14.097 --> 00:41:16.395
I have rights
and I demand to see my lawyer...

568
00:41:16.557 --> 00:41:19.481
...before you press that small button
on the side firmly.

569
00:41:19.644 --> 00:41:20.315
Press it.

570
00:41:25.650 --> 00:41:28.654
That, gentlemen,
is a standard-issue neuralyser.

571
00:41:28.820 --> 00:41:30.288
You're not gonna remember that.

572
00:41:30.446 --> 00:41:33.199
And just because you see
a black man driving a nice car...

573
00:41:33.366 --> 00:41:35.664
...does not mean it's stolen.

574
00:41:38.496 --> 00:41:42.217
I stole that one.
But not because I'm black.

575
00:41:45.169 --> 00:41:46.921
I'll be done with the car in a minute!

576
00:41:47.088 --> 00:41:50.683
Just find it and take it back
to the jerk at the Roosevelt Hotel.

577
00:42:05.523 --> 00:42:07.491
Where is the Archanan?

578
00:42:07.650 --> 00:42:08.742
You are too late.

579
00:42:08.943 --> 00:42:11.571
He is going to give the humans...

580
00:42:11.738 --> 00:42:12.409
...the Arc Net.

581
00:42:14.532 --> 00:42:16.534
Let's agree to disagree.

582
00:42:47.315 --> 00:42:48.658
We'll take it from here.

583
00:42:49.067 --> 00:42:50.444
K?

584
00:42:52.070 --> 00:42:54.118
K! K!

585
00:43:10.254 --> 00:43:12.052
Dad, I'm on Earth.

586
00:43:12.215 --> 00:43:13.842
I need bail.

587
00:43:23.017 --> 00:43:26.396
<i>Will the owner of a blue
warp-speed cruiser...</i>

588
00:43:26.562 --> 00:43:28.985
<i>...please report to the front desk.</i>

589
00:43:31.943 --> 00:43:36.494
You need to turn the electricity
down on that damn thing.

590
00:43:36.656 --> 00:43:38.829
Can't taste my fricking tongue, K.

591
00:43:38.991 --> 00:43:40.117
How do you know my name?

592
00:43:42.120 --> 00:43:44.464
What? Because I called you "K"?

593
00:43:45.123 --> 00:43:46.750
No, I call everybody K.

594
00:43:47.291 --> 00:43:48.668
It's kind of my thing.

595
00:43:48.835 --> 00:43:50.007
What up, K?

596
00:43:50.253 --> 00:43:51.470
All right, I sort of--

597
00:43:53.297 --> 00:43:56.892
Yeah, that's kind of my thing.
I just-- Some people like it.

598
00:43:57.051 --> 00:43:59.179
Most people.

599
00:43:59.387 --> 00:44:00.980
Now that I know what you look like...

600
00:44:01.139 --> 00:44:02.766
...when you're lying, show me...

601
00:44:02.932 --> 00:44:05.310
...what you look like
when you're telling the truth?

602
00:44:06.060 --> 00:44:08.688
I won those at Coney Island
on the ring toss.

603
00:44:08.896 --> 00:44:11.274
I won a stuffed bear once,
but never one of these.

604
00:44:11.566 --> 00:44:13.318
Must be good, slick.

605
00:44:13.651 --> 00:44:16.200
All right, sir,
I was minding my own business.

606
00:44:16.362 --> 00:44:18.535
I was waiting for my girl,
who, by the way...

607
00:44:18.698 --> 00:44:21.326
...is probably worried sick
looking for me right now.

608
00:44:21.492 --> 00:44:24.496
So I just need my things
and I need to get back to her.

609
00:44:24.662 --> 00:44:25.584
What's her name?

610
00:44:27.123 --> 00:44:28.420
Your gal, what's her name?

611
00:44:29.834 --> 00:44:31.336
Schtaron.

612
00:44:33.838 --> 00:44:35.215
Schtaron?

613
00:44:39.510 --> 00:44:41.933
I bet Schtaron likes that suit of yours.

614
00:44:42.847 --> 00:44:44.770
What, it's a crime to wear a black suit?

615
00:44:45.016 --> 00:44:47.815
All right, listen.
I haven't done anything wrong.

616
00:44:48.019 --> 00:44:50.442
And I need to get out of here.
I cannot be with you.

617
00:44:50.605 --> 00:44:54.781
Terribly sorry. X is frightfully upset
about the whole Coney Island incident.

618
00:44:54.942 --> 00:44:56.444
Thanks for the heads-up.

619
00:44:58.029 --> 00:45:00.828
Oh, man, this coffee tastes like dirt.

620
00:45:00.990 --> 00:45:03.743
- What do you expect? It was--
- Just ground this morning.

621
00:45:04.702 --> 00:45:05.498
O?

622
00:45:09.707 --> 00:45:11.675
No, I call ladies "O."

623
00:45:11.834 --> 00:45:14.883
To me, O is feminine, K is masculine.

624
00:45:15.046 --> 00:45:19.552
You know, I see a couple,
I'm like, "O-Κ."

625
00:45:19.717 --> 00:45:22.095
What a mess. Any casualties?

626
00:45:22.303 --> 00:45:24.180
Yes, Roman the Fabulist.

627
00:45:24.347 --> 00:45:26.600
Any human casualties?

628
00:45:27.225 --> 00:45:28.898
No, sir.

629
00:45:29.894 --> 00:45:31.191
Whο the hell is this?

630
00:45:31.604 --> 00:45:32.776
Look, I was--

631
00:45:32.939 --> 00:45:35.943
- Stray human caught in the net.
- Code 43 him and throw him back.

632
00:45:36.108 --> 00:45:38.202
You're late for a meeting
with the Viagrans.

633
00:45:38.361 --> 00:45:40.489
They have a revolutionary new pill.

634
00:45:40.655 --> 00:45:41.827
It's really...

635
00:45:43.532 --> 00:45:44.704
Okay, slick.

636
00:45:47.411 --> 00:45:48.663
I was waiting for my girl.

637
00:45:48.829 --> 00:45:49.876
Schtaron.

638
00:45:50.039 --> 00:45:52.713
Yes, she's Greek.

639
00:45:53.918 --> 00:45:58.219
Okay. Just one last thing.
An eye exam.

640
00:46:03.594 --> 00:46:06.438
That's not an eye exam, K.
That's a big-ass neuralyser!

641
00:46:06.597 --> 00:46:09.771
You have a lot of information for
a fella who doesn't know anything.

642
00:46:09.934 --> 00:46:11.311
I see what you're saying.

643
00:46:11.894 --> 00:46:13.862
You know, Κ, we need to hold up a second.

644
00:46:14.021 --> 00:46:15.238
K!

645
00:46:16.107 --> 00:46:17.780
Let's get this bite guard in here.

646
00:46:17.942 --> 00:46:19.694
Hey, back up, back up.

647
00:46:20.778 --> 00:46:23.622
K, listen, I think we got off
on the wrong foot, all right?

648
00:46:23.781 --> 00:46:26.125
So let's just stop for a second and talk.

649
00:46:26.284 --> 00:46:28.002
Don't put me in here, K!

650
00:46:28.160 --> 00:46:29.332
Too late, hoss.

651
00:46:29.495 --> 00:46:32.499
K, no, listen to me.
I can help you with this case!

652
00:46:33.457 --> 00:46:34.800
K!

653
00:46:36.127 --> 00:46:38.346
I'm doing the truth face!
You're missing it!

654
00:46:38.754 --> 00:46:40.347
I'll just use my imagination.

655
00:46:43.801 --> 00:46:44.768
K, the killer...

656
00:46:44.927 --> 00:46:47.646
...you're looking for, I'm after
the same guy. A Boglodite.

657
00:46:47.805 --> 00:46:48.852
His name is Boris.

658
00:46:49.015 --> 00:46:50.141
Ship has sailed, amigo.

659
00:46:50.308 --> 00:46:52.060
If we don't get him, there'll be two.

660
00:46:52.310 --> 00:46:54.153
You had my undivided attention.

661
00:46:54.312 --> 00:46:55.438
One will have one arm...

662
00:46:55.604 --> 00:46:57.322
...and one's gonna have two. K!

663
00:46:57.481 --> 00:46:58.824
Listen to me!

664
00:46:58.983 --> 00:46:59.950
If you erase me...

665
00:47:00.109 --> 00:47:01.361
...you erase the world!

666
00:47:03.321 --> 00:47:04.243
<i>Fifteen seconds...</i>

667
00:47:04.405 --> 00:47:06.624
<i>...to neuralysation. Fourteen.</i>

668
00:47:07.408 --> 00:47:09.456
<i>Thirteen. Twelve.</i>

669
00:47:09.618 --> 00:47:12.542
<i>Eleven. Ten. Nine.</i>

670
00:47:12.705 --> 00:47:17.632
When you see Boris tomorrow, K,
kill him. Do not arrest him, kill him!

671
00:47:18.002 --> 00:47:20.846
<i>Four. Three. Two.</i>

672
00:47:27.511 --> 00:47:31.266
Is this thing off?
Hey, I dοn't think it's all the way off, K!

673
00:47:31.766 --> 00:47:33.768
It's whirring and buzzing.

674
00:47:34.602 --> 00:47:36.900
I don't know if I don't know nothing.

675
00:47:40.858 --> 00:47:42.280
I knew Roman.

676
00:47:42.568 --> 00:47:45.321
His wife cooked me dinner once.
While it was not pleasant...

677
00:47:45.488 --> 00:47:46.990
...he was my friend.

678
00:47:47.531 --> 00:47:50.159
Last chance, who are you
and what do you know?

679
00:47:55.373 --> 00:47:56.340
I'm an agent...

680
00:47:56.499 --> 00:47:58.126
...from the future. We're partners.

681
00:47:58.292 --> 00:47:59.965
In 25 years, you'll recruit me...

682
00:48:00.127 --> 00:48:03.222
...and 14 years after that,
the guy you didn't let me kill today...

683
00:48:03.381 --> 00:48:05.383
...escapes from prison,
jumps to the past...

684
00:48:05.549 --> 00:48:09.224
...and unleashes an invasion of Earth.
We got about 19 hours to kill him...

685
00:48:09.387 --> 00:48:12.061
...so, really, we need to go right now.

686
00:48:20.064 --> 00:48:20.781
All right.

687
00:48:26.487 --> 00:48:28.239
So that's the story you believe.

688
00:48:28.406 --> 00:48:29.453
That one was the truth.

689
00:48:29.615 --> 00:48:31.709
Wasn't the whole truth,
but it'll do for now.

690
00:48:31.867 --> 00:48:34.996
What are you talking about?
Of course it's the whole truth.

691
00:48:35.162 --> 00:48:38.382
The problem with a lie is once
you start lying you put yourself...

692
00:48:42.336 --> 00:48:43.929
Agent K.

693
00:48:44.505 --> 00:48:45.802
What's he still doing here?

694
00:48:46.006 --> 00:48:48.805
I might have cooked him too long.
Thought I'd walk him out.

695
00:48:48.968 --> 00:48:50.811
I put my pants on.

696
00:48:56.517 --> 00:48:58.019
Okay, future man, where to?

697
00:48:59.520 --> 00:49:00.612
I don't know.

698
00:49:00.771 --> 00:49:01.772
What do you mean?

699
00:49:03.941 --> 00:49:07.821
I don't know.
Go wherever you went last time.

700
00:49:07.987 --> 00:49:10.410
I haven't been here.
I didn't tell you where I went?

701
00:49:10.614 --> 00:49:13.993
No. I mean, we don't really talk.

702
00:49:14.910 --> 00:49:18.335
What kind of partners sit in a car
every day for 14 years and don't talk?

703
00:49:18.956 --> 00:49:23.086
Exactly. And this is the type
of problem it causes.

704
00:49:23.252 --> 00:49:24.299
It's dysfunctional.

705
00:49:24.545 --> 00:49:28.641
All right, sport, you better get useful
real quick or you go back in room 43.

706
00:49:30.092 --> 00:49:31.344
Man...

707
00:49:34.805 --> 00:49:37.649
There was something in the file
about a factory.

708
00:49:37.808 --> 00:49:39.981
Something happened at a factory.

709
00:49:41.979 --> 00:49:45.825
Hey, look, man, you can put
your Jedi Knight on me all you want.

710
00:49:45.983 --> 00:49:47.235
That's all I got.

711
00:49:52.573 --> 00:49:53.665
That spark something?

712
00:49:53.866 --> 00:49:56.540
Roman had this on his person
when he was murdered.

713
00:49:59.038 --> 00:49:59.709
It's a matchbook.

714
00:49:59.914 --> 00:50:01.757
No, it's a clue.

715
00:50:01.957 --> 00:50:03.584
He didn't smoke.

716
00:50:33.239 --> 00:50:35.162
You lose something over here, Hondo?

717
00:50:35.533 --> 00:50:36.910
No.

718
00:50:37.076 --> 00:50:39.374
Hey, man, how old are you?

719
00:50:41.997 --> 00:50:43.089
Twenty-nine.

720
00:50:43.999 --> 00:50:45.501
You got some city miles on you.

721
00:50:46.293 --> 00:50:49.297
I'm starting to understand
why we don't talk.

722
00:50:56.178 --> 00:50:58.897
- How well do you know this place?
- I know its reputation.

723
00:50:59.348 --> 00:51:03.023
I don't like it. I hate going in blind.
I'm gonna need my gun.

724
00:51:03.686 --> 00:51:05.438
Sure thing, slick.

725
00:51:05.604 --> 00:51:08.027
K! Wait, no, I gotta go in
with you!

726
00:51:08.274 --> 00:51:09.992
You sit tight. I'll be fine.

727
00:51:10.150 --> 00:51:12.323
Wait, no! No!

728
00:51:12.486 --> 00:51:13.282
K!

729
00:51:13.445 --> 00:51:16.164
K, don't go in by yourself!

730
00:51:18.826 --> 00:51:19.702
Hi, fellas.

731
00:51:21.996 --> 00:51:23.373
Need to see the boss.

732
00:51:23.706 --> 00:51:24.878
He's busy.

733
00:51:26.041 --> 00:51:28.089
Well, I'm gonna just take a look around.

734
00:51:33.799 --> 00:51:36.222
Looks like we have ourselves a standoff.

735
00:51:36.385 --> 00:51:38.353
Looks that way.

736
00:51:42.308 --> 00:51:45.482
- Still keep the key under the ashtray.
- Lucky guess.

737
00:51:45.644 --> 00:51:47.191
Now, where were we?

738
00:51:47.354 --> 00:51:49.231
I was about to tell you to screw off.

739
00:51:49.398 --> 00:51:51.275
Hey, slick, you bowl in the future?

740
00:51:51.442 --> 00:51:53.615
MiB league champ, three years running.

741
00:51:53.777 --> 00:51:55.450
Well, let's see it.

742
00:51:56.405 --> 00:51:57.657
You did not walk into my...

743
00:51:57.823 --> 00:51:59.621
...establishment
and rip my head off!

744
00:51:59.783 --> 00:52:03.287
My man, we don't have a lot of time.
You really need to tell him something.

745
00:52:03.454 --> 00:52:05.127
I'll tell him this!

746
00:52:05.289 --> 00:52:06.290
All right, your head.

747
00:52:06.457 --> 00:52:10.462
Wait. Hey, if you do this,
I am gonna hunt you down...

748
00:52:10.628 --> 00:52:11.800
...and make sure you...

749
00:52:11.962 --> 00:52:13.464
...walk funny for the rest...

750
00:52:13.631 --> 00:52:15.725
...of your miserable last days
on Earth!

751
00:52:16.800 --> 00:52:17.801
Tough spare, slick.

752
00:52:17.968 --> 00:52:19.220
You messed with the wrong head!

753
00:52:19.386 --> 00:52:21.559
- His head's a little...
- You gonna tell us...

754
00:52:21.722 --> 00:52:23.224
...where Dom is?

755
00:52:23.390 --> 00:52:25.688
I'll kill you both.
I'll kill both of youse!

756
00:52:28.020 --> 00:52:30.273
Your hook's a little off.
Want me to clean her?

757
00:52:30.439 --> 00:52:32.066
- Sure thing.
- No, no, no.

758
00:52:32.733 --> 00:52:35.987
Come on, I just cleaned
the bathroom with this thing!

759
00:52:36.153 --> 00:52:37.450
No cleaning! No cleaning!

760
00:52:37.613 --> 00:52:41.618
Okay! Okay, all right!
All right, he's in the back.

761
00:52:41.784 --> 00:52:44.378
But he's not gonna talk
to Men in Black scum like you.

762
00:52:44.536 --> 00:52:46.209
Now give me back my head.

763
00:52:46.789 --> 00:52:49.759
K, I call this one
"Low Hanging Fruit."

764
00:52:49.958 --> 00:52:51.210
That ain't a finger hole...

765
00:52:51.377 --> 00:52:53.095
...you sick bastard!

766
00:52:53.253 --> 00:52:54.425
I'll pop your head off...

767
00:52:54.588 --> 00:52:55.965
...and see how you like it.

768
00:52:58.592 --> 00:52:59.844
I'm gonna kill both of you!

769
00:53:00.260 --> 00:53:02.308
I'm gonna kill the both of youse!

770
00:53:02.471 --> 00:53:03.973
I'll kill you both!

771
00:53:07.476 --> 00:53:10.446
- Well, we're on the right track.
- Just the wrong train.

772
00:53:10.813 --> 00:53:12.156
If he had any secrets...

773
00:53:12.314 --> 00:53:13.816
...I'm guessing he spilled them.

774
00:53:13.982 --> 00:53:16.360
A smart man figures out
what victims have in common.

775
00:53:16.527 --> 00:53:18.029
A smart man wοuld.

776
00:53:18.195 --> 00:53:19.617
That's a big-ass phone.

777
00:53:20.155 --> 00:53:22.874
- Don't put that up to your head.
- Agent O.

778
00:53:23.033 --> 00:53:25.456
How's your day been, Agent K?

779
00:53:25.619 --> 00:53:26.745
Fair to middling.

780
00:53:26.912 --> 00:53:27.913
How are things going?

781
00:53:28.080 --> 00:53:29.297
<i>Very good, thank you.</i>

782
00:53:29.456 --> 00:53:31.208
Hey, you saw her like an hour ago.

783
00:53:31.375 --> 00:53:33.594
I need cleanup and containment
at cosmic Lanes.

784
00:53:33.752 --> 00:53:35.675
Listen, I got a dead Parlaxian.

785
00:53:35.838 --> 00:53:38.557
Now Roman was a Byvoid,
correct me if I'm wrong...

786
00:53:38.716 --> 00:53:42.346
- ...from the same planetary grouping?
- <i>A system in the Triangulum Galaxy...</i>

787
00:53:42.511 --> 00:53:43.763
...wiped out by Boglodites.

788
00:53:43.929 --> 00:53:45.146
Wasn't the third planet--?

789
00:53:45.305 --> 00:53:47.057
- Glamouria?
- <i>Glamouria.</i>

790
00:53:48.726 --> 00:53:49.818
Thank you, Miss O.

791
00:53:50.894 --> 00:53:53.397
I know where Boris is headed to next.

792
00:53:53.564 --> 00:53:58.161
You were close, slick.
It's not a factory, it's the Factory.

793
00:54:02.030 --> 00:54:05.079
Look, if Boris turns out
to be here, I'm gonna kill him...

794
00:54:05.242 --> 00:54:07.791
- ...I need my gun.
- No deal.

795
00:54:09.705 --> 00:54:11.207
I've been an agent for 14 years.

796
00:54:11.373 --> 00:54:14.923
Which means I'm the senior agent
on this case. Now, I hate to pull rank...

797
00:54:15.085 --> 00:54:17.133
...but I am instructing
my junior agent...

798
00:54:17.296 --> 00:54:20.220
...that's you, to give me my gun
right now. That's an order.

799
00:54:27.181 --> 00:54:28.649
No, no, no, space gun.

800
00:54:28.807 --> 00:54:30.229
You're welcome.

801
00:54:31.185 --> 00:54:32.687
I didn't say thank you.

802
00:54:38.776 --> 00:54:41.279
For such an ungainly species,
they've thrived on Earth.

803
00:54:41.445 --> 00:54:43.038
I was an agent for three years...

804
00:54:43.197 --> 00:54:45.245
...before I realised
all models were aliens.

805
00:54:45.407 --> 00:54:47.580
Found out the hard way.

806
00:54:47.951 --> 00:54:48.702
Password?

807
00:54:48.911 --> 00:54:51.539
Hey, look, funky '60s dude,
we don't have a lot of time.

808
00:54:51.705 --> 00:54:53.002
Janis Joplin.

809
00:55:01.298 --> 00:55:03.721
Is there anybody here who's not an alien?

810
00:55:09.056 --> 00:55:10.148
Very nice.

811
00:55:10.808 --> 00:55:11.934
Blink. That's good.

812
00:55:12.142 --> 00:55:13.064
Look in the camera.

813
00:55:13.393 --> 00:55:15.270
Is that Andy Warhol?

814
00:55:17.147 --> 00:55:18.364
Yep.

815
00:55:20.400 --> 00:55:23.620
Excuse me, Mr. Warhol,
could we have a minute?

816
00:55:23.779 --> 00:55:26.999
Now is not a good time.
This is a be-in.

817
00:55:27.491 --> 00:55:28.333
Just a few...

818
00:55:28.492 --> 00:55:29.744
...questions.

819
00:55:29.910 --> 00:55:33.084
No questions. No answers.

820
00:55:33.247 --> 00:55:34.874
Just being.

821
00:55:35.249 --> 00:55:37.468
We have an urgent matter
to discuss with you...

822
00:55:37.626 --> 00:55:39.469
...regarding one
of your party guests.

823
00:55:40.838 --> 00:55:42.306
Why don't you come back...

824
00:55:42.464 --> 00:55:44.466
...next week, after the happening...

825
00:55:44.633 --> 00:55:46.431
...has happened.

826
00:55:47.302 --> 00:55:50.431
Sorry, Mr. Warhol. You like
talking slow. We got stuff to do.

827
00:55:50.597 --> 00:55:51.814
I've got a planet to save.

828
00:55:52.724 --> 00:55:54.397
You're distressing. Everything...

829
00:55:54.560 --> 00:55:56.153
...about you upsets me.

830
00:55:59.982 --> 00:56:02.030
Damn it, K!
Are you trying to blow my cover?

831
00:56:02.192 --> 00:56:03.910
Agent W, your cover is safe.

832
00:56:04.194 --> 00:56:05.912
Whoa, Andy Warhol is one of us?

833
00:56:06.071 --> 00:56:06.913
Safe?

834
00:56:07.072 --> 00:56:09.074
You out of your mind?
I'm so out of ideas...

835
00:56:09.241 --> 00:56:11.460
...I'm painting cans
and bananas for chrissakes.

836
00:56:11.702 --> 00:56:14.376
Actually, Mr. Warhol,
I gotta tell you, I love your work.

837
00:56:14.621 --> 00:56:15.873
Oh, thank you.

838
00:56:16.039 --> 00:56:16.961
Whο's the dumb-ass?

839
00:56:18.125 --> 00:56:20.298
How about a little
professional courtesy here?

840
00:56:20.460 --> 00:56:21.757
- Dumb-ass.
- Say it again.

841
00:56:21.920 --> 00:56:23.092
- Want me to?
- I dare you.

842
00:56:23.255 --> 00:56:24.051
Dumb-ass.

843
00:56:24.214 --> 00:56:25.887
- Agents.
- I have no problem...

844
00:56:26.049 --> 00:56:28.393
...pimp-slapping the shiznit
out of Andy Warhol.

845
00:56:29.052 --> 00:56:29.723
What?

846
00:56:35.309 --> 00:56:36.561
Why are you looking at me?

847
00:56:39.313 --> 00:56:41.657
Oh, all right. You know what?
Agent K...

848
00:56:41.815 --> 00:56:44.489
...you see what information
you can get from Agent W...

849
00:56:44.651 --> 00:56:46.870
...and I'll go case the perimeter.

850
00:56:47.029 --> 00:56:48.747
- That work for everybody?
- Go do that.

851
00:56:48.906 --> 00:56:50.374
- How about that?
- Oh, cute.

852
00:56:50.532 --> 00:56:52.409
- Okay.
- Very nice.

853
00:56:52.659 --> 00:56:55.003
Someone forget his nap?

854
00:57:02.836 --> 00:57:04.679
Hey, how you doing?

855
00:57:05.839 --> 00:57:07.307
Chilling.

856
00:57:12.554 --> 00:57:13.271
Who's that guy?

857
00:57:13.513 --> 00:57:15.186
Don't tell me he's your new partner.

858
00:57:15.349 --> 00:57:18.944
Actually, he's my old partner.
He travelled back from the future--

859
00:57:19.102 --> 00:57:21.230
Stop, don't tell me.
I don't want to know.

860
00:57:21.396 --> 00:57:23.194
Andy, Yoko's here.

861
00:57:23.357 --> 00:57:25.234
Yoko's here.

862
00:57:26.360 --> 00:57:30.661
Tell her that I'm filming this man
eating a hamburger.

863
00:57:31.198 --> 00:57:33.417
It's transcendent.

864
00:57:33.742 --> 00:57:35.995
All right, now the pickle.

865
00:57:43.335 --> 00:57:44.757
What are you doing on my turf?

866
00:57:45.170 --> 00:57:46.513
Tracking a killer. Boglodite.

867
00:57:46.672 --> 00:57:49.221
We believe he's gonna
hit here next, a Glamourian.

868
00:57:49.383 --> 00:57:52.432
Glamourian?
Right solar system, wrong planet.

869
00:57:52.594 --> 00:57:54.141
He's gotta be after the Archanan.

870
00:57:54.304 --> 00:57:55.556
Archanans are extinct.

871
00:57:55.722 --> 00:57:58.646
Apparently not.
One washed ashore last week.

872
00:57:58.892 --> 00:58:01.987
The whole Roswell circuit's
all abuzz about it.

873
00:58:02.312 --> 00:58:04.565
Alien unicorn. Last of its species.

874
00:58:05.232 --> 00:58:06.279
His name's Griffin.

875
00:58:06.733 --> 00:58:08.827
<i>Griffin the Archanan.</i>

876
00:58:10.570 --> 00:58:11.617
How's it going?

877
00:58:11.780 --> 00:58:15.250
Going? Ηow's it going? That depends.
For me, personally, things are good.

878
00:58:15.409 --> 00:58:16.911
Unless we're in the future...

879
00:58:17.077 --> 00:58:19.421
...where the muscle boy argues
with his girlfriend.

880
00:58:19.579 --> 00:58:22.458
She storms off and bumps the guy
with the stuffed mushrooms...

881
00:58:22.624 --> 00:58:24.718
...who dumps the tray
on the sailors on leave.

882
00:58:24.876 --> 00:58:26.128
A shoving match breaks out.

883
00:58:26.294 --> 00:58:29.138
They crash into the table.
In which case, I gotta move my plate.

884
00:58:33.343 --> 00:58:36.142
Or it's the future where
the pastrami sandwich I'm eating...

885
00:58:36.304 --> 00:58:38.022
...causes me gastric distress.

886
00:58:38.181 --> 00:58:40.809
Thankfully, your friend offers
the antacids he carries...

887
00:58:40.976 --> 00:58:43.820
...in his right pocket, so good.
I'll be good.

888
00:58:43.979 --> 00:58:46.949
Except in the future where
I have to leave in two minutes...

889
00:58:47.107 --> 00:58:49.530
...before he has a chance
to offer me the antacids...

890
00:58:49.693 --> 00:58:52.697
...so on the whole, I'd have to say
not good. I am not good.

891
00:58:54.865 --> 00:58:56.538
But that depends.

892
00:58:58.618 --> 00:58:59.915
K!

893
00:59:00.412 --> 00:59:01.629
How will we find this guy?

894
00:59:01.788 --> 00:59:03.540
What am I, a schmuck?

895
00:59:04.041 --> 00:59:04.712
He's here?

896
00:59:04.875 --> 00:59:07.924
"Here" is a relative term.
He's a fifth dimensional being.

897
00:59:08.086 --> 00:59:10.384
They can live in and visualise
an infinite set...

898
00:59:10.547 --> 00:59:12.766
...of time-space probabilities
simultaneously.

899
00:59:13.300 --> 00:59:14.847
Sounds like fun. Good work.

900
00:59:15.010 --> 00:59:16.478
Whοa, whoa, K, K, K.

901
00:59:17.971 --> 00:59:20.269
You gotta fake my death, okay?

902
00:59:20.432 --> 00:59:22.526
I can't listen to sitar music anymore.

903
00:59:22.809 --> 00:59:25.403
All right, I'll see what I can do.
I'll talk to X.

904
00:59:25.562 --> 00:59:27.690
K, I can't tell the women from the men.

905
00:59:27.856 --> 00:59:29.073
May I see your watch?

906
00:59:29.733 --> 00:59:30.985
Oh, it is 7:18.

907
00:59:31.359 --> 00:59:33.862
No, no, your other watch,
the one your father gave you.

908
00:59:35.739 --> 00:59:37.833
How do you know about my father's watch?

909
00:59:41.495 --> 00:59:42.747
Oh, dear.

910
00:59:43.163 --> 00:59:44.881
This is the one where Roman is dead...

911
00:59:45.040 --> 00:59:47.668
...and the gentleman at the
bowling alley. So much death.

912
00:59:47.834 --> 00:59:51.304
Such an infinitesimally
small chance for success.

913
00:59:52.172 --> 00:59:53.173
K!

914
00:59:53.381 --> 00:59:54.052
Griffin, right?

915
00:59:55.050 --> 00:59:55.721
We're here--

916
00:59:55.884 --> 00:59:57.010
Because of Boris.

917
00:59:57.219 --> 00:59:58.391
We think he's coming--

918
00:59:58.553 --> 01:00:00.146
To kill me.
He'll be here in minutes...

919
01:00:00.347 --> 01:00:01.348
...unless we're in...

920
01:00:01.515 --> 01:00:02.983
...the future
where he made the lights...

921
01:00:03.141 --> 01:00:04.142
...and is about...

922
01:00:04.309 --> 01:00:05.526
...to shoot from the door...

923
01:00:05.685 --> 01:00:07.028
...in which case we're all dead.

924
01:00:09.439 --> 01:00:11.567
Good, that was a close one.

925
01:00:11.733 --> 01:00:13.155
K, I need a space gun.

926
01:00:13.610 --> 01:00:14.406
The Βoglodites...

927
01:00:14.569 --> 01:00:15.991
...consume any planet
in their path.

928
01:00:16.154 --> 01:00:17.451
Mine, Roman's, the Parlaxians'.

929
01:00:17.614 --> 01:00:21.460
I tried to stop them, but if we stop
them here, if we deny them Earth...

930
01:00:21.618 --> 01:00:23.746
...we can stop them.
They'll starve before...

931
01:00:23.912 --> 01:00:25.004
...they reach the next planet.

932
01:00:27.874 --> 01:00:29.091
Sixty-three seconds.

933
01:00:29.501 --> 01:00:30.844
How do we do that? Stop them?

934
01:00:31.545 --> 01:00:33.218
What?

935
01:00:33.713 --> 01:00:35.681
Sorry. I have something for you.

936
01:00:35.841 --> 01:00:38.014
A gift. It can protect you.

937
01:00:38.718 --> 01:00:42.222
I had to hide it from Boris,
but if you find me again...

938
01:00:42.889 --> 01:00:44.687
...I'll give it to you.

939
01:00:44.891 --> 01:00:48.521
Thank you. What a game!
Amazing! It's a real miracle!

940
01:00:48.812 --> 01:00:50.359
What do you mean? What miracle?

941
01:00:50.522 --> 01:00:52.115
Thirty seconds. I have to go.

942
01:00:52.274 --> 01:00:53.241
No, we got you.

943
01:00:53.400 --> 01:00:55.823
Negative possibilities are
multiplying as we speak.

944
01:00:55.986 --> 01:00:57.283
- Okay.
- Twenty seconds.

945
01:00:57.445 --> 01:00:58.116
All right.

946
01:00:58.280 --> 01:00:59.247
We got it, relax.

947
01:00:59.406 --> 01:01:01.579
If your watch is broken
and I have gastric--

948
01:01:01.741 --> 01:01:04.494
Fly! Find your place in the world!

949
01:01:04.661 --> 01:01:06.334
Oh, dear.

950
01:01:06.538 --> 01:01:08.461
Boris is coming through that door...

951
01:01:08.623 --> 01:01:09.340
...in 12...

952
01:01:09.499 --> 01:01:11.126
...11, 10--

953
01:01:11.334 --> 01:01:12.085
Wait!

954
01:01:12.252 --> 01:01:13.845
Did you have chocolate milk?

955
01:01:15.088 --> 01:01:15.759
Yes.

956
01:01:16.840 --> 01:01:17.887
Cindy.

957
01:01:19.426 --> 01:01:20.222
K!

958
01:01:20.385 --> 01:01:21.227
- Griffin!
- Got him.

959
01:01:30.437 --> 01:01:31.563
Damn it!

960
01:01:50.957 --> 01:01:52.425
I'm good, I'm good.

961
01:01:52.584 --> 01:01:53.801
What you got?

962
01:01:54.711 --> 01:01:56.964
Damn it! We had him!

963
01:01:57.214 --> 01:01:59.091
Relax, Cochise. We'll find him.

964
01:01:59.883 --> 01:02:01.556
First of all, my name is J, okay?

965
01:02:01.718 --> 01:02:04.642
It's not "son," it's not "slick"
and it damn sure ain't no "Cochise."

966
01:02:04.971 --> 01:02:07.724
I'm not gonna relax because
we're running out of time...

967
01:02:07.891 --> 01:02:09.484
...and there's an invasion coming.

968
01:02:09.643 --> 01:02:12.613
You're not really recognising
my voicial intensity.

969
01:02:14.231 --> 01:02:16.233
But there was one guy who could help.

970
01:02:16.483 --> 01:02:18.451
Hey, Griffin! Griffin! Where's Griffin?

971
01:02:19.486 --> 01:02:21.284
Griffin. Where's Griffin at, Κ?

972
01:02:21.571 --> 01:02:25.496
He's gone. If Boris gets to him
before we do, that's no bueno.

973
01:02:25.909 --> 01:02:27.126
We need pie.

974
01:02:27.452 --> 01:02:29.830
- What?
- My granddaddy always said:

975
01:02:29.996 --> 01:02:32.215
"If you got a problem you can't solve...

976
01:02:32.374 --> 01:02:34.547
...it helps to get out
of your head." Pie.

977
01:02:35.335 --> 01:02:36.086
- Pie?
- Yeah.

978
01:02:36.253 --> 01:02:37.880
Your granddaddy, heavyset man?

979
01:02:38.338 --> 01:02:40.636
- A little bit.
- Yeah, you know what?

980
01:02:40.799 --> 01:02:42.346
We've been doing smart stuff:

981
01:02:42.509 --> 01:02:44.682
We've been following clues,
doing police work.

982
01:02:44.928 --> 01:02:46.976
It might be time we do something stupid.

983
01:02:47.514 --> 01:02:50.108
Something that ain't got
nothing to do with nothing.

984
01:02:50.267 --> 01:02:52.190
Now, I want some pie, K.
I want some pie.

985
01:02:52.352 --> 01:02:53.729
Let's go get dumb-ass pie.

986
01:02:54.354 --> 01:02:55.822
Sounds good.

987
01:03:25.885 --> 01:03:26.807
Have any specials?

988
01:03:27.554 --> 01:03:30.854
He'll have what he always has after
he reads the menu for 10 minutes...

989
01:03:31.016 --> 01:03:32.438
...and asks about specials.

990
01:03:32.600 --> 01:03:35.274
A slice of apple pie
with a nasty piece of cheddar.

991
01:03:35.437 --> 01:03:36.984
I'll have the strawberry-rhubarb.

992
01:03:37.147 --> 01:03:38.899
It's my last meal, I'm gonna splurge.

993
01:03:42.402 --> 01:03:45.827
World-class serial killer out there
and we're having pie.

994
01:03:46.031 --> 01:03:48.500
What do you do in your spare time, stretch?

995
01:03:49.576 --> 01:03:53.376
See, I sense you're not embracing
the concept here.

996
01:03:53.538 --> 01:03:55.586
Pie don't work unless you let it.

997
01:03:55.749 --> 01:03:57.126
I'm gonna let it.

998
01:03:57.292 --> 01:03:58.669
And you say we don't talk?

999
01:03:59.336 --> 01:04:02.215
You go ahead. Ask me any question.
Anything you want.

1000
01:04:02.380 --> 01:04:06.101
As long as it doesn't have to do
with the case. Just let her rip.

1001
01:04:08.094 --> 01:04:09.937
What's up with you and O?

1002
01:04:11.431 --> 01:04:12.102
Me and O?

1003
01:04:13.266 --> 01:04:14.688
Yeah, you and O.

1004
01:04:14.851 --> 01:04:16.194
All right, all right.

1005
01:04:16.394 --> 01:04:18.067
All right, this is it.

1006
01:04:19.356 --> 01:04:22.701
A while back, I was assigned
to keep tabs on a musician.

1007
01:04:22.942 --> 01:04:23.738
Mick Jagger?

1008
01:04:23.902 --> 01:04:26.075
He's in this British band,
the Rolling Stones.

1009
01:04:26.363 --> 01:04:27.330
Rings a bell.

1010
01:04:27.489 --> 01:04:30.789
We believed he was on the planet
to breed with Earth women.

1011
01:04:30.992 --> 01:04:34.212
So I was in London and that's when I met O.

1012
01:04:34.371 --> 01:04:38.342
Just smart. Funny. A great smile.

1013
01:04:39.459 --> 01:04:42.588
And we find ourselves in this pub,
which is a bar, all right?

1014
01:04:42.754 --> 01:04:46.759
Warm beer and the worst food you ever ate.

1015
01:04:47.133 --> 01:04:50.683
We just played darts till the sun came up.

1016
01:04:50.845 --> 01:04:52.563
Neither of us wanted to leave.

1017
01:05:01.981 --> 01:05:04.075
What the hell happened to you, man?

1018
01:05:04.484 --> 01:05:06.953
I don't know. It hasn't happened yet.

1019
01:05:07.112 --> 01:05:11.037
Come on, what about you, slick?
In the future, you got yourself a girl?

1020
01:05:11.658 --> 01:05:12.955
I got you.

1021
01:05:13.118 --> 01:05:15.792
I cannot believe this,
freaking New York Mets.

1022
01:05:15.954 --> 01:05:17.331
Total losers!

1023
01:05:17.497 --> 01:05:19.295
It's a rough time to be a Mets fan.

1024
01:05:19.457 --> 01:05:22.006
Tell me about it.
Never gonna catch the Cubs.

1025
01:05:22.335 --> 01:05:25.339
That's funny. The Mets actually
win it all this year.

1026
01:05:25.588 --> 01:05:26.931
Oh, yeah.

1027
01:05:27.173 --> 01:05:27.969
No, I'm serious.

1028
01:05:28.133 --> 01:05:28.850
I'm sure.

1029
01:05:29.008 --> 01:05:31.557
Look, three months from now,
yοur buddies down there...

1030
01:05:31.719 --> 01:05:33.892
...are gonna be calling them
the Amazing Mets...

1031
01:05:34.055 --> 01:05:36.558
...and the Miracle Mets.

1032
01:05:38.351 --> 01:05:40.069
What?

1033
01:05:40.228 --> 01:05:41.901
What you got there, hoss?

1034
01:05:42.939 --> 01:05:47.365
The Archanan said, "It's amazing!
It's a miracle! I'll see you at the game."

1035
01:05:48.528 --> 01:05:49.905
I know where he is.

1036
01:05:50.697 --> 01:05:52.699
Told you to trust the pie.

1037
01:05:57.036 --> 01:06:00.540
If Griffin's here for a game,
he's either too early or too late.

1038
01:06:00.707 --> 01:06:04.052
He's here. We just gotta find him
before Βoris does.

1039
01:06:11.301 --> 01:06:13.224
It's time to give you your things back...

1040
01:06:13.386 --> 01:06:14.478
...partner.

1041
01:06:14.721 --> 01:06:16.769
You get some pie in you, you get all mushy.

1042
01:06:16.931 --> 01:06:19.104
I'm just tired of carrying your stuff.

1043
01:06:20.393 --> 01:06:22.691
Come on now! All right! Let's go...

1044
01:06:22.854 --> 01:06:23.730
...Mets!

1045
01:06:23.897 --> 01:06:26.400
Let's go, Mets! Let's go...

1046
01:06:26.566 --> 01:06:28.785
- ...Mets! Let's go, Met--
- Griffin?

1047
01:06:31.488 --> 01:06:32.956
You're just in time!

1048
01:06:33.114 --> 01:06:37.460
Unless this is the one where Robinson
bad-hops it past third, it's almost over.

1049
01:06:39.579 --> 01:06:40.956
Are we missing something?

1050
01:06:41.748 --> 01:06:42.965
The game.

1051
01:07:11.611 --> 01:07:14.831
So this is how you see things?
This is amazing.

1052
01:07:14.989 --> 01:07:18.710
It's a gigantic pain in the ass.
But it has its moments.

1053
01:07:19.202 --> 01:07:21.250
This game doesn't happen till October.

1054
01:07:21.412 --> 01:07:22.755
It's always October...

1055
01:07:22.997 --> 01:07:24.590
...and November and March.

1056
01:07:24.749 --> 01:07:27.753
So many futures, and all real.
Don't know which will coalesce.

1057
01:07:27.919 --> 01:07:29.717
Until then, they're all happening.

1058
01:07:29.879 --> 01:07:32.849
Like this one, it's my favourite moment
in human history.

1059
01:07:33.007 --> 01:07:36.386
All the things that had to converge
for the Mets to win the World Series.

1060
01:07:36.553 --> 01:07:39.727
They were in last place every single
season until they won it all.

1061
01:07:39.889 --> 01:07:41.186
You said you had a gift.

1062
01:07:41.349 --> 01:07:42.191
That baseball...

1063
01:07:42.350 --> 01:07:46.275
...thrown for the last out of game five,
manufactured in '62 by Spalding...

1064
01:07:46.437 --> 01:07:49.907
...of Chicopee, Massachusetts,
was aerodynamically flawed...

1065
01:07:50.066 --> 01:07:52.410
...due to the horsehide
being improperly tanned...

1066
01:07:52.569 --> 01:07:54.412
...because the tanner's wife
left him...

1067
01:07:54.571 --> 01:07:56.073
...for a Puerto Rican golf pro--

1068
01:07:56.239 --> 01:07:57.741
The gift?

1069
01:07:57.907 --> 01:08:00.160
Oh, yes, of course. In the box.

1070
01:08:04.163 --> 01:08:07.007
It's the surprise.
To protect the Earth.

1071
01:08:07.166 --> 01:08:08.042
It's a shield.

1072
01:08:12.755 --> 01:08:13.426
Shield.

1073
01:08:14.966 --> 01:08:17.515
Archanan. Arc Net.
Yοu put up the Arc Net.

1074
01:08:17.677 --> 01:08:19.429
- How?
- When that ball is pitched to...

1075
01:08:19.596 --> 01:08:20.438
...Davey Johnson...

1076
01:08:20.597 --> 01:08:21.814
<i>...who became a player...</i>

1077
01:08:21.973 --> 01:08:25.443
<i>...because his dad couldn't find a
football to give him for his birthday...</i>

1078
01:08:25.602 --> 01:08:26.353
<i>...it hits...</i>

1079
01:08:26.519 --> 01:08:28.487
<i>...his bat two micrometres
too high...</i>

1080
01:08:28.646 --> 01:08:29.989
<i>...popping out to Cleon Jones...</i>

1081
01:08:30.815 --> 01:08:33.068
<i>...who would've been born Clara,
a statistical...</i>

1082
01:08:33.276 --> 01:08:36.746
<i>...typist, if his parents didn't have
an extra glass of wine that night...</i>

1083
01:08:36.904 --> 01:08:38.781
<i>...before going to bed.</i>

1084
01:08:40.033 --> 01:08:40.955
<i>A miracle...</i>

1085
01:08:41.117 --> 01:08:43.620
...is what seems impossible
but happens anyway.

1086
01:08:53.046 --> 01:08:54.514
I lost my planet.

1087
01:08:54.714 --> 01:08:57.092
I don't want you to lose yours.

1088
01:08:57.258 --> 01:08:59.761
It'll take a miracle,
but if you pull this off...

1089
01:08:59.969 --> 01:09:01.971
...you'll be my new
favourite moment...

1090
01:09:02.138 --> 01:09:03.981
...in human history.

1091
01:09:04.140 --> 01:09:05.608
Oh, dear.

1092
01:09:06.059 --> 01:09:07.686
I forgot to see this one coming.

1093
01:09:14.776 --> 01:09:15.868
Damn it!

1094
01:09:26.037 --> 01:09:27.209
Have these in the future?

1095
01:09:27.372 --> 01:09:28.464
No.

1096
01:09:28.706 --> 01:09:29.707
Get on.

1097
01:09:33.461 --> 01:09:35.463
Keep gyro settings at zero gain.

1098
01:09:35.630 --> 01:09:38.224
Balance pitch and yaw
with bursts on the centre stalk...

1099
01:09:38.383 --> 01:09:39.760
...between 80 and 100 psi.

1100
01:09:40.259 --> 01:09:41.260
I didn't understand...

1101
01:09:41.427 --> 01:09:42.849
...any of that!

1102
01:09:43.012 --> 01:09:45.106
- Gyro at zero gain.
- It is.

1103
01:09:45.264 --> 01:09:47.642
Pitch and yaw with short bursts
on the centre stalk.

1104
01:09:47.809 --> 01:09:48.480
I did!

1105
01:09:48.643 --> 01:09:50.611
Between 80 and 100 psi!

1106
01:09:51.646 --> 01:09:52.693
Got it.

1107
01:09:55.316 --> 01:09:57.193
The Arc Net! Give it to me!

1108
01:09:57.360 --> 01:09:59.237
This isn't the one where you get it!

1109
01:09:59.404 --> 01:10:01.498
- All right there, chief?
- Hell, yeah.

1110
01:10:01.656 --> 01:10:03.203
It'd be better with four wheels!

1111
01:10:03.366 --> 01:10:04.709
Twο is, like, my minimum.

1112
01:10:11.624 --> 01:10:14.093
What happens if Boris gets the Arc Net?

1113
01:10:14.252 --> 01:10:16.505
Boglodite invasion,
total destruction of Earth!

1114
01:10:40.695 --> 01:10:42.413
The box!

1115
01:10:53.624 --> 01:10:54.876
Good boy.

1116
01:10:55.293 --> 01:10:56.795
We gotta stop this guy!

1117
01:10:59.046 --> 01:10:59.922
I've been trying!

1118
01:11:00.131 --> 01:11:01.474
You haven't been trying?

1119
01:11:02.008 --> 01:11:02.679
Hey, slick.

1120
01:11:03.009 --> 01:11:06.058
In the future,
we ever do the Texas two-step?

1121
01:11:06.220 --> 01:11:07.893
Yes, sir!

1122
01:11:33.331 --> 01:11:34.298
Did you get him?

1123
01:11:34.624 --> 01:11:36.092
Give me a sec.

1124
01:11:40.505 --> 01:11:41.381
Is he dead?

1125
01:11:41.839 --> 01:11:43.216
Negative.

1126
01:11:44.091 --> 01:11:45.308
He got away.

1127
01:11:47.762 --> 01:11:49.605
I got Griffin. Let's get out of here.

1128
01:12:04.362 --> 01:12:06.456
I feel younger already.

1129
01:12:32.682 --> 01:12:36.107
You pathetic waste of Boglodite flesh.

1130
01:12:36.269 --> 01:12:39.569
I'd kill you right now,
if I didn't value my own life.

1131
01:12:39.814 --> 01:12:41.612
- Who are you?
- Look at you.

1132
01:12:41.774 --> 01:12:44.823
Every mistake I've ever made,
just waiting to happen.

1133
01:12:44.986 --> 01:12:46.158
What happened to my arm?

1134
01:12:46.320 --> 01:12:48.573
You lose it, shot off by a human.

1135
01:12:48.739 --> 01:12:50.207
No human could defeat me.

1136
01:12:50.575 --> 01:12:54.830
You spend the next 40 years in prison,
chained up like an animal.

1137
01:12:54.996 --> 01:12:56.873
No prison can hold me!

1138
01:12:57.039 --> 01:12:59.758
They built one especially for us,
on the moon.

1139
01:13:00.084 --> 01:13:01.882
No human has been to the moon...

1140
01:13:02.044 --> 01:13:04.718
...so they cannot have
built it there already.

1141
01:13:04.881 --> 01:13:07.885
Stop arguing! You can avoid
all of that if you just listen to me!

1142
01:13:08.050 --> 01:13:11.680
You were defeated!
You let it get shot off!

1143
01:13:11.846 --> 01:13:14.645
That wasn't me, that was you!

1144
01:13:19.937 --> 01:13:20.904
What's your plan?

1145
01:13:21.188 --> 01:13:23.361
Prevent the Arc Net from being deployed.

1146
01:13:23.524 --> 01:13:26.073
- Kill anyone who tries.
- Good plan.

1147
01:13:26.569 --> 01:13:27.536
Didn't work.

1148
01:13:27.695 --> 01:13:28.662
With my help...

1149
01:13:28.905 --> 01:13:31.784
...we'll get the Arc Net,
kill Agent K...

1150
01:13:31.949 --> 01:13:34.247
...the invasion will be successful...

1151
01:13:34.452 --> 01:13:35.999
...and we'll get to keep both...

1152
01:13:36.162 --> 01:13:38.540
...of our Ar--! Stop...

1153
01:13:38.706 --> 01:13:40.208
...staring at it!

1154
01:13:41.125 --> 01:13:42.217
Listen.

1155
01:13:57.558 --> 01:14:00.812
- You all right?
- Yeah. Thank you for saving my life.

1156
01:14:01.103 --> 01:14:02.025
It's what we do.

1157
01:14:03.105 --> 01:14:04.357
You still have the Arc Net?

1158
01:14:06.567 --> 01:14:08.740
When you're being hunted
by Boris the Animal...

1159
01:14:08.903 --> 01:14:10.621
...you get good at hiding things.

1160
01:14:36.013 --> 01:14:38.107
This will save your world.

1161
01:14:41.018 --> 01:14:43.191
Once it's outside the atmosphere,
it gets...

1162
01:14:43.354 --> 01:14:44.651
...a whole lot bigger.

1163
01:14:45.856 --> 01:14:47.699
All you have to do is deploy it.

1164
01:14:48.776 --> 01:14:52.201
You mean in space?
Well, how do you suppose we do that?

1165
01:14:52.363 --> 01:14:55.037
It's just one small step.

1166
01:15:09.547 --> 01:15:10.594
The moon launch.

1167
01:15:14.051 --> 01:15:15.724
Cape Canaveral.

1168
01:15:17.054 --> 01:15:19.933
July 16th, 1969.

1169
01:15:20.307 --> 01:15:21.900
We got six hours to get to Florida.

1170
01:15:22.226 --> 01:15:23.603
Better get a move on, slick.

1171
01:15:23.894 --> 01:15:24.861
Wait, hοld up.

1172
01:15:25.021 --> 01:15:27.149
Not us.
I'm gonna do this one alone.

1173
01:15:27.314 --> 01:15:28.236
He has to be the--

1174
01:15:28.399 --> 01:15:29.275
Griffin.

1175
01:15:29.442 --> 01:15:30.568
What do you mean, alone?

1176
01:15:31.318 --> 01:15:33.195
I'm gonna go to Florida.
You stay here.

1177
01:15:33.362 --> 01:15:34.614
I need you to trust me.

1178
01:15:35.072 --> 01:15:38.793
Trust you? I don't think so.
Something you're not telling me, slick?

1179
01:15:38.951 --> 01:15:40.419
You're not going to Florida.

1180
01:15:40.578 --> 01:15:42.330
That ain't gonna happen, partner.

1181
01:15:42.496 --> 01:15:43.873
Look, K...

1182
01:15:44.415 --> 01:15:46.713
...please, I will not allow you
to go to Florida.

1183
01:15:48.836 --> 01:15:49.553
Stop me.

1184
01:15:54.759 --> 01:15:56.181
Yοu die there!

1185
01:15:58.929 --> 01:16:02.024
Cape Canaveral. Apollo launch.

1186
01:16:03.934 --> 01:16:05.777
Boris kills you there.

1187
01:16:08.189 --> 01:16:09.736
That's what I'm here for.

1188
01:16:10.357 --> 01:16:11.859
That's what I came back to stop.

1189
01:16:12.068 --> 01:16:14.036
Oh, dear. We're in this one.

1190
01:16:16.363 --> 01:16:17.330
K...

1191
01:16:18.074 --> 01:16:20.202
...I saw the file,
I looked at the report.

1192
01:16:20.367 --> 01:16:21.584
I said I told you everything--

1193
01:16:23.204 --> 01:16:24.751
That's for lying to me.

1194
01:16:24.997 --> 01:16:26.044
Look, I'm sorry, man!

1195
01:16:29.126 --> 01:16:30.844
That's for telling me the truth!

1196
01:16:32.129 --> 01:16:34.006
I'm trying to protect you...

1197
01:16:35.216 --> 01:16:36.684
...man!

1198
01:16:38.719 --> 01:16:41.393
The bitterest truth is better
than the sweetest lies.

1199
01:16:45.142 --> 01:16:46.985
He has to go to Cape Canaveral.

1200
01:16:47.144 --> 01:16:49.897
He must deploy the Arc Net
as he did before.

1201
01:16:50.064 --> 01:16:51.566
There's no other way.

1202
01:16:52.149 --> 01:16:55.323
K is the only hope in saving Earth.

1203
01:16:56.153 --> 01:16:57.700
Can I save him?

1204
01:16:58.572 --> 01:17:02.372
Is there any future where I save his life?

1205
01:17:04.829 --> 01:17:06.627
Yes.

1206
01:17:08.165 --> 01:17:10.384
But where there is death...

1207
01:17:11.335 --> 01:17:13.758
...there will always be death.

1208
01:17:31.605 --> 01:17:33.448
According to you, I've done this before.

1209
01:17:33.607 --> 01:17:35.029
So we know it's possible.

1210
01:17:35.192 --> 01:17:37.160
If you're half the agent you say you are...

1211
01:17:37.319 --> 01:17:39.617
...you'll make sure
I don't get killed doing it.

1212
01:17:44.034 --> 01:17:46.002
So are we partners? You tell me.

1213
01:17:48.873 --> 01:17:50.466
Let's go.

1214
01:18:03.554 --> 01:18:04.476
Agent K...

1215
01:18:04.638 --> 01:18:06.060
- ...how are you?
- I'm good.

1216
01:18:06.223 --> 01:18:09.397
Okay, group hug on the way
to doing what we're doing.

1217
01:18:09.560 --> 01:18:13.781
<i>This morning, man is about to launch
himself on a trip to the moon...</i>

1218
01:18:13.939 --> 01:18:16.442
<i>...with the expectation
of landing there.</i>

1219
01:18:16.609 --> 01:18:18.077
Look, I gotta ask you.

1220
01:18:18.235 --> 01:18:20.613
If we pull this off,
fix things the way they were...

1221
01:18:20.779 --> 01:18:22.577
...O and I, are we...?

1222
01:18:22.740 --> 01:18:23.957
A wise man once told me...

1223
01:18:24.116 --> 01:18:26.915
...don't ask questions you don't
want to know the answer to.

1224
01:18:28.245 --> 01:18:30.919
- I said that, didn't I?
- Yes, sir.

1225
01:18:35.586 --> 01:18:37.054
Here they are.

1226
01:18:37.922 --> 01:18:40.050
- What are they?
- Jetpacks.

1227
01:18:40.216 --> 01:18:41.763
Jetpacks?

1228
01:18:42.843 --> 01:18:45.596
No, no, no.
We're not doing jetpacks.

1229
01:18:45.763 --> 01:18:48.107
There's a reason we don't
have these in the future.

1230
01:18:48.265 --> 01:18:49.266
K, we gotta drive.

1231
01:18:49.683 --> 01:18:52.653
Can't drive to Florida from Manhattan
in five hours, chief.

1232
01:18:52.937 --> 01:18:56.862
Yeah, we can. The red button,
standard issue in every MiB car.

1233
01:18:57.024 --> 01:18:58.901
Press the red button, goes into hyperdrive.

1234
01:18:59.068 --> 01:19:00.866
No red buttons yet, slick.

1235
01:19:02.613 --> 01:19:04.741
Come on, man.

1236
01:19:09.828 --> 01:19:10.670
Do you know...

1237
01:19:10.829 --> 01:19:12.126
...how to work this thing?

1238
01:19:12.289 --> 01:19:14.417
It's like with anything.

1239
01:19:14.583 --> 01:19:18.508
Just have to strap yourself in,
hope for the best.

1240
01:19:19.630 --> 01:19:20.927
Isn't that right, Miss O?

1241
01:19:22.299 --> 01:19:24.301
Unfortunately, it is.

1242
01:19:35.479 --> 01:19:36.776
You ready, slick?

1243
01:19:38.649 --> 01:19:40.196
Let's get it.

1244
01:19:40.401 --> 01:19:42.244
This is gonna be interesting!

1245
01:19:55.165 --> 01:19:57.463
<i>It's just minutes to the...</i>

1246
01:19:57.668 --> 01:19:59.295
<i>...historic launch of Apollo 11...</i>

1247
01:19:59.461 --> 01:20:01.805
<i>...with all going well.</i>

1248
01:20:18.188 --> 01:20:21.362
I'm so glad this isn't
one of the times we explode.

1249
01:20:21.608 --> 01:20:23.326
One of the times?

1250
01:20:26.155 --> 01:20:27.702
Oh, we got company.

1251
01:20:32.244 --> 01:20:33.712
The hell?

1252
01:20:35.289 --> 01:20:37.257
Is that a battery belt?

1253
01:20:47.134 --> 01:20:48.681
All right, I got it.

1254
01:20:51.889 --> 01:20:54.438
No, any reality
that gets the shield deployed...

1255
01:20:54.641 --> 01:20:56.393
...is one where you tell the truth.

1256
01:20:56.769 --> 01:20:58.146
The truth?

1257
01:20:58.479 --> 01:21:00.481
The truth is the only path.

1258
01:21:00.689 --> 01:21:02.362
This is a restricted area!

1259
01:21:07.404 --> 01:21:09.372
Yes, sir, it is.

1260
01:21:09.531 --> 01:21:12.501
Good day, gentlemen.
Great day for America, isn't it?

1261
01:21:12.659 --> 01:21:16.334
My name is Agent J.
This is Agent K. That's Griff.

1262
01:21:16.497 --> 01:21:18.591
We're from a secret government
organisation...

1263
01:21:18.749 --> 01:21:22.344
...that polices and monitors
alien activity on and off planet Earth.

1264
01:21:23.754 --> 01:21:24.880
Here's the thing.

1265
01:21:25.047 --> 01:21:27.516
We have this special little metal thingy...

1266
01:21:27.674 --> 01:21:31.474
...that Griff gave us that we have
to get on top of that rocket...

1267
01:21:31.637 --> 01:21:35.267
...to prevent an alien invasion.

1268
01:21:38.685 --> 01:21:39.652
That worked.

1269
01:21:39.812 --> 01:21:42.531
- Like a charm.
- Sir, Delta Gate. We have a problem.

1270
01:21:42.856 --> 01:21:46.235
Three trespassers. No IDs,
but they've got weapons, sir.

1271
01:21:46.443 --> 01:21:48.616
Some kind I've never seen before.

1272
01:21:56.370 --> 01:21:57.917
What breed of fool do you have to be...

1273
01:21:58.080 --> 01:22:01.004
...to penetrate my site
on the day of the most massive feat...

1274
01:22:01.166 --> 01:22:02.418
...attempted by mankind?

1275
01:22:02.584 --> 01:22:05.508
Watched by God, the population
οf the planet and my own...

1276
01:22:05.671 --> 01:22:06.797
- ...firstborn!
- Colonel?

1277
01:22:07.714 --> 01:22:08.840
Colonel, they had these.

1278
01:22:10.008 --> 01:22:12.181
They said they needed
to put something on the rocket...

1279
01:22:12.344 --> 01:22:13.516
...for an invasion.

1280
01:22:17.724 --> 01:22:18.725
Thanks.

1281
01:22:18.934 --> 01:22:20.186
I got 10 minutes to launch.

1282
01:22:20.436 --> 01:22:24.486
If you pose a threat to that rocket,
you tell me now and do not lie to me.

1283
01:22:28.902 --> 01:22:30.904
I told the truth last time.

1284
01:22:35.909 --> 01:22:37.707
Sir, this man came here from...

1285
01:22:37.911 --> 01:22:39.288
...the future to protect me...

1286
01:22:39.455 --> 01:22:42.880
...so I can attach a shield to the top
of that rocket and save the world.

1287
01:22:43.041 --> 01:22:45.009
I need your help to do that.

1288
01:22:48.172 --> 01:22:49.469
Take them to the brig.

1289
01:22:49.631 --> 01:22:51.133
You're slipping, Griff.

1290
01:22:51.675 --> 01:22:52.847
Sir, if I may.

1291
01:23:09.109 --> 01:23:09.780
Corporal.

1292
01:23:11.195 --> 01:23:12.538
You men are no longer needed.

1293
01:23:13.030 --> 01:23:14.156
I'll take the prisoners.

1294
01:23:14.531 --> 01:23:16.374
- Sir, are you--?
- Dismissed.

1295
01:23:25.209 --> 01:23:26.210
Follow me.

1296
01:23:33.592 --> 01:23:35.765
You did the future thing.
What did you show him?

1297
01:23:35.928 --> 01:23:38.056
Only what he needed to see.

1298
01:23:39.389 --> 01:23:40.766
I have to go now.

1299
01:23:41.892 --> 01:23:43.314
What? No, no, no. Come on.

1300
01:23:43.727 --> 01:23:45.229
You don't need me anymore.

1301
01:23:45.646 --> 01:23:48.024
All right, Griff,
don't start flipping on me.

1302
01:23:48.190 --> 01:23:51.660
When Boris' arm is taken, the past
will be as it was. K will survive.

1303
01:23:51.818 --> 01:23:53.786
He will not know you were ever here.

1304
01:23:55.489 --> 01:23:59.585
All right. Arm gone, got it.
Like a reset?

1305
01:23:59.743 --> 01:24:02.997
When that happens, go home.
Leave.

1306
01:24:03.163 --> 01:24:03.834
You coming?

1307
01:24:03.997 --> 01:24:05.999
Yeah, all right!

1308
01:24:07.960 --> 01:24:10.429
Thanks, man.
Hey, will I ever see you again?

1309
01:24:10.671 --> 01:24:12.469
Anything's possible.

1310
01:24:15.092 --> 01:24:16.469
Oh, Griff.

1311
01:24:22.766 --> 01:24:25.269
I can never bear to watch this part.

1312
01:24:27.187 --> 01:24:28.860
<i>Armstrong and Aldrin are scheduled...</i>

1313
01:24:29.022 --> 01:24:30.945
<i>...to set foot on the moon...</i>

1314
01:24:31.108 --> 01:24:35.079
<i>...on early Monday morning,
Εastern Daylight Τime.</i>

1315
01:24:36.446 --> 01:24:37.197
Where's Griffin?

1316
01:24:37.406 --> 01:24:39.158
Doing his own thing.

1317
01:25:01.805 --> 01:25:02.522
Gentlemen.

1318
01:25:06.602 --> 01:25:08.855
This elevator will take you to the top.

1319
01:25:09.021 --> 01:25:11.023
To get the Arc Net
outside the atmosphere...

1320
01:25:11.189 --> 01:25:14.193
...you need to strap it to the escape
rocket above the capsule!

1321
01:25:14.359 --> 01:25:15.736
You do not want to be...

1322
01:25:15.902 --> 01:25:18.155
...anywhere near this rocket
when it takes off!

1323
01:25:18.322 --> 01:25:20.700
- Questions?
- No. Thank you for this, colonel.

1324
01:25:20.866 --> 01:25:22.459
Some job you got there.

1325
01:25:22.701 --> 01:25:23.873
Hey, thanks a lot, bro.

1326
01:25:24.036 --> 01:25:26.539
What did Griff show you back there?

1327
01:25:26.705 --> 01:25:28.127
How important you are.

1328
01:25:28.457 --> 01:25:30.050
You and your partner.

1329
01:25:38.300 --> 01:25:40.723
If everything goes right
the way we hope it does...

1330
01:25:40.886 --> 01:25:43.639
...I'm gonna end up
getting out of here pretty quick...

1331
01:25:43.805 --> 01:25:47.230
...so I'm not gonna have a chance
to say a proper goodbye.

1332
01:25:47.392 --> 01:25:50.942
If things go wrong,
not gonna have a chance to, either.

1333
01:25:52.898 --> 01:25:54.525
So I guess win or lose, this is it.

1334
01:25:59.071 --> 01:26:00.948
I see why I recruited you.

1335
01:26:03.825 --> 01:26:04.917
You're a good man.

1336
01:26:08.413 --> 01:26:10.040
Good man.

1337
01:26:12.501 --> 01:26:14.754
Man, what the hell happened to you?

1338
01:26:15.170 --> 01:26:17.514
I told you, it still hasn't happened yet.

1339
01:26:22.344 --> 01:26:24.062
I'll take this one!

1340
01:26:24.429 --> 01:26:25.555
Naughty.

1341
01:26:28.266 --> 01:26:30.314
Get a pedicure if you get a second.

1342
01:26:40.237 --> 01:26:42.365
And liftoff.

1343
01:27:23.822 --> 01:27:25.540
<i>Just passed the two-minute mark...</i>

1344
01:27:25.699 --> 01:27:29.169
<i>...in the countdown, and all is still go
as we monitor our status board.</i>

1345
01:27:50.474 --> 01:27:53.273
<i>Astronauts report it feels good.
Power transfer is complete.</i>

1346
01:27:54.019 --> 01:27:56.989
<i>Neil Armstrong just reported back
it's been a smooth countdown.</i>

1347
01:28:09.576 --> 01:28:10.623
Hey!

1348
01:28:10.869 --> 01:28:12.496
Boris, can you give me a hand?

1349
01:28:12.662 --> 01:28:14.460
Hey.

1350
01:28:19.169 --> 01:28:19.920
Hey!

1351
01:28:20.879 --> 01:28:22.506
You hear me calling you?

1352
01:28:23.381 --> 01:28:24.883
Boris the Animal!

1353
01:28:25.383 --> 01:28:26.054
Hey!

1354
01:28:26.218 --> 01:28:28.391
Boris the Animal!

1355
01:28:30.263 --> 01:28:32.641
It's just Boris!

1356
01:28:36.478 --> 01:28:37.525
You're gonna lose.

1357
01:28:37.813 --> 01:28:39.065
Let's agree to disagree.

1358
01:28:58.708 --> 01:28:59.880
Hey!

1359
01:29:00.919 --> 01:29:02.546
Boris the Animal!

1360
01:29:12.514 --> 01:29:13.310
Right.

1361
01:29:14.140 --> 01:29:14.811
Left.

1362
01:29:42.878 --> 01:29:43.800
You're gonna lose.

1363
01:29:43.962 --> 01:29:46.010
Let's agree to disagree.

1364
01:29:54.890 --> 01:29:56.267
Hey!

1365
01:29:56.975 --> 01:29:58.773
Boris the Animal!

1366
01:30:05.692 --> 01:30:06.409
Right.

1367
01:30:06.776 --> 01:30:08.323
Left. Left.

1368
01:30:09.404 --> 01:30:10.155
Right.

1369
01:30:14.242 --> 01:30:16.210
That's not possible.

1370
01:30:16.494 --> 01:30:18.417
Let's agree to disagree.

1371
01:30:24.127 --> 01:30:26.801
That's not possible!

1372
01:30:36.097 --> 01:30:37.098
K!

1373
01:30:38.767 --> 01:30:41.111
I win! I'm better than me!

1374
01:30:48.526 --> 01:30:49.778
That's my partner.

1375
01:30:50.236 --> 01:30:52.079
That's my partner!

1376
01:30:58.286 --> 01:30:59.333
If we call this in...

1377
01:30:59.496 --> 01:31:02.170
- ...they'll scrub the launch.
- I didn't see anything.

1378
01:31:36.866 --> 01:31:38.743
- Where's your partner?
- He went home.

1379
01:31:38.910 --> 01:31:40.412
- How does that work?
- Yοu got me.

1380
01:31:40.578 --> 01:31:41.875
Come on!

1381
01:31:56.720 --> 01:31:57.516
Get down!

1382
01:32:28.585 --> 01:32:29.928
Bingo.

1383
01:32:30.837 --> 01:32:32.931
Man, that is some next-level stuff.

1384
01:32:42.932 --> 01:32:44.275
You ever want to see more...

1385
01:32:44.476 --> 01:32:47.776
...I know a top-secret organisation
that could use a man like you.

1386
01:32:49.689 --> 01:32:51.362
I wish I could.

1387
01:32:51.941 --> 01:32:52.908
Thank you.

1388
01:32:53.526 --> 01:32:55.403
I'll see you around, K.

1389
01:32:57.155 --> 01:32:57.826
Look out!

1390
01:33:03.119 --> 01:33:04.792
Go ahead.

1391
01:33:05.038 --> 01:33:06.790
Arrest me.

1392
01:33:08.374 --> 01:33:10.047
Not this time.

1393
01:33:20.053 --> 01:33:23.057
"Where there's death,
there will always be death."

1394
01:33:32.398 --> 01:33:35.652
Daddy! Daddy!

1395
01:33:39.739 --> 01:33:40.535
Hey.

1396
01:33:41.574 --> 01:33:43.542
Hey, my name's K.
What's your name?

1397
01:33:44.077 --> 01:33:45.124
James.

1398
01:33:45.286 --> 01:33:47.835
James? That's a nice name.

1399
01:33:48.039 --> 01:33:49.382
Where's my dad?

1400
01:33:52.252 --> 01:33:54.129
What have you got there?
What is that?

1401
01:33:54.295 --> 01:33:55.672
My dad gave it to me.

1402
01:33:55.839 --> 01:33:58.092
We timed the launch.

1403
01:34:05.223 --> 01:34:07.021
Where is my daddy?

1404
01:34:11.104 --> 01:34:12.526
He...

1405
01:34:13.106 --> 01:34:16.861
He went to go do something very special.

1406
01:34:17.026 --> 01:34:18.903
And he wanted me...

1407
01:34:19.070 --> 01:34:23.416
...to stay here and take care
of his best pal.

1408
01:34:28.288 --> 01:34:30.461
When is he gonna be back?

1409
01:34:31.624 --> 01:34:33.001
He...

1410
01:34:47.807 --> 01:34:49.275
James...

1411
01:34:50.643 --> 01:34:52.441
...if you look right here...

1412
01:34:52.604 --> 01:34:55.824
...I will tell you the only thing
you ever need to know.

1413
01:35:01.321 --> 01:35:03.119
Your daddy is a hero.

1414
01:35:03.323 --> 01:35:05.792
My daddy is a hero?

1415
01:35:08.995 --> 01:35:12.295
- Want to take a walk with me?
- Yes.

1416
01:35:21.841 --> 01:35:23.138
James?

1417
01:36:05.510 --> 01:36:07.183
You're late.

1418
01:36:07.345 --> 01:36:09.598
Sorry. Lost track of time.

1419
01:36:11.557 --> 01:36:12.774
How do you know that song?

1420
01:36:13.142 --> 01:36:15.190
Drink your coffee.
We got work to do.

1421
01:36:16.062 --> 01:36:17.860
What do you know and what do you don't?

1422
01:36:18.022 --> 01:36:19.740
How do I know what I don't know?

1423
01:36:19.899 --> 01:36:22.823
That's a really good question.
Did we go to Wu's last night?

1424
01:36:22.986 --> 01:36:23.737
Yeah.

1425
01:36:24.070 --> 01:36:24.946
Boglodites?

1426
01:36:25.113 --> 01:36:25.909
Extinct for 40 years.

1427
01:36:26.322 --> 01:36:28.575
Perfect. Did we talk
on the phone last night?

1428
01:36:28.741 --> 01:36:29.993
You hung up on me.

1429
01:36:30.410 --> 01:36:32.037
Yeah, I did.

1430
01:36:33.079 --> 01:36:35.252
But that was because
of all those secrets...

1431
01:36:35.790 --> 01:36:38.714
...the universe doesn't know about.

1432
01:36:43.423 --> 01:36:44.219
But...

1433
01:36:44.590 --> 01:36:46.388
...I've realised that...

1434
01:36:46.551 --> 01:36:49.054
...last night was a long...

1435
01:36:49.220 --> 01:36:51.518
...long time ago.

1436
01:36:55.768 --> 01:36:58.521
And, really, I just want to say thank you.

1437
01:36:59.105 --> 01:37:01.107
It's been my privilege.

1438
01:37:10.950 --> 01:37:13.373
You know, there's a really
high possibility now...

1439
01:37:13.536 --> 01:37:16.130
...that I might know some things
you don't know.

1440
01:37:16.289 --> 01:37:17.882
I doubt it.

1441
01:37:18.041 --> 01:37:20.009
I bet I know what went down with you and O.

1442
01:37:20.168 --> 01:37:22.091
She's a fine lady, but you know the rules.

1443
01:37:22.253 --> 01:37:24.426
There's no fraternising amongst agents.

1444
01:37:24.589 --> 01:37:27.308
I think y'all might have fraternised
a time or two.

1445
01:37:30.470 --> 01:37:33.815
This is my new favourite moment
in human history.

1446
01:37:33.973 --> 01:37:37.227
Unless this is the one
where Κ forgot to leave a tip.

1447
01:37:51.824 --> 01:37:53.701
Almost forgot.

1448
01:38:02.251 --> 01:38:03.969
That was a close one.
